bcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130381#post1130381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well considering that most lines do not yet have a corebook yet, werewolf is fine with its one supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love Werewolf, but Mage 2E has to this day ( over a year past premiere ) only corebook and it's much more need Signs of Sorcery ( i.e. corebook 2E, part II ), than Werewolf needed The Pack ( even than I am most glad we have Pack, it's awesome book! )<br /> <br /> I also would point out that Promethean did not had written info in brochure about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1120196-night-horrors-the-tormented\">Night Horrors: The Tormented</a>, even if PtC gameline still get's it - so there maybe some Werewolf supprise later this year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:14:32-07:00","id":1130392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130370#post1130370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf hasn't really gone longer than any other given line without a supplement. And it's gotten quite a lot of Dark Eras love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't count Dark Eras, as it's a catch all for every line. Sure it's extra content, but it's not the same as a stand alone supplement. Granted I love The Pack, so there is that.<br /> <br /> Having said that, Werewolf is woefully underrepresented at Cons in comparison to other products, which is depressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-17-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:38:33-07:00","id":1130410,"title":"","content":"Changeling is in even worse position....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:40:07-07:00","id":1130412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130392#post1130392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't count Dark Eras, as it's a catch all for every line. Sure it's extra content, but it's not the same as a stand alone supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it catches every line is exactly why people should count it in their reconning of supplementary material for the various lines. There are a whopping 10 and soon to be 11 game lines in CofD alone, which is itself a fraction of the material OPP produces. Compilations like Dark Eras are really the only way to insure content gets realeased for all of them regularly. And yet, when this same topic pops up in every subforum every few months, no one ever takes Dark Eras and the like into account, even when it's pointed out that, if you exclude Dark Eras, no 2e line has seen more than one book published in a year. Werewolf is not by any means unique in this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:41:52-07:00","id":1130413,"title":"","content":"Well, your game is 2e while several of them aren't, and it already has a supplement, which is more than some can say. Not to defend this company at all, but this is a pretty silly reason to attack them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:05:31-07:00","id":1130423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130412#post1130412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, when this same topic pops up in every subforum every few months, no one ever takes Dark Eras and the like into account, even when it's pointed out that, if you exclude Dark Eras, no 2e line has seen more than one book published in a year. Werewolf is not by any means unique in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon the Descent did. And while Secrets of the Covenants didn't come out in the same year as Thousand Years of Night, They did come out in the same 12 month period, and there's a third vampire book being art directed at this moment. I suppose technically you could balance that out by mentioning that the first Dark Eras had very little Vampire material.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting subject.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can really hold it against Stew that he works on both Werewolf lines. Most of the Apocalypse content that's been coming out has been Kickstarter stuff, and a few developers work on multiple lines. Matt McFarland did Demon, Beast, and Promethean. Dave Brookshaw is doing Mage and Deviant. Rose Bailey developed the Chronicles of Darkness core and Vampire, though I believe she stepped back a bit on the latter.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, we really don't see him much on the forums compared to the other developers and that does make him seem like more of a distant person, in regards to the game, though expecting people to post on the forum is kind of longshot to begin with, this not being anyone's full time job and all. Arguably one of the reasons mage is so popular is that Dave had gone to such lengths to talk about it, including talking about things that aren't in books and might never be in books. At the very least, when taking part of the forums, it gives developers a clear picture of 'what readers want' in terms of content and 'what readers need' in terms of rules and clarity. For instance, if the last Dark Eras Kickstarter has shown us anything, it's that people really glom on to mentions of events that happened in a gamelines past, like with the mages of Nassau. While looking at the forum you can see a lot of questions about 'end game' werewolves, and more explanation for rules regarding Influence.<br /> <br /> And not being a part of things we don't really hear when something is coming down the line.<br /> <br /> As a fan, not getting a nice influx of new books, or even one announced at something like GenCon is a major bummer. But I don't think they'd give up the line. It sells well, people respond to it, people like it just as much as any other Chronicles game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:10:12-07:00","id":1130425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130413#post1130413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, your game is 2e while several of them aren't, and it already has a supplement, which is more than some can say. Not to defend this company at all, but this is a pretty silly reason to attack them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please respect the conversation. If you don't like the thread, you're under no obligation to post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:12:56-07:00","id":1130428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130425#post1130425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please respect the conversation. If you don't like the thread, you aren't obliged to post.</div> </div> </div> </div>A conversation can have rebuttals. <br /> <br /> I'm a Mummy fan who's also played a lot of Geist. To hear someone feel 'abandoned' when their game has an updated core and its first supplement while these games won't be up to the new edition for at least another year or two feels a little bit oblivious to the state of other gamelines out there, as does the nonsensical &quot;Dark Eras doesn't count as content!&quot; statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:13:05-07:00","id":1130430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130412#post1130412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it catches every line is exactly why people should count it in their reconning of supplementary material for the various lines. There are a whopping 10 and soon to be 11 game lines in CofD alone, which is itself a fraction of the material OPP produces. Compilations like Dark Eras are really the only way to insure content gets realeased for all of them regularly. And yet, when this same topic pops up in every subforum every few months, no one ever takes Dark Eras and the like into account, even when it's pointed out that, if you exclude Dark Eras, no 2e line has seen more than one book published in a year. Werewolf is not by any means unique in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eras is just setting material. The only thing of use I've got was meager fleshing out of the Pure. And I mean, meager in the extreme (should've been included in the Corebook). For a game based almost exclusively on antagonists; the game needs to put emphasis on them already.<br /> <br /> Instead we got what, fantastic pregnancy rules and conditions. *eyeroll*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-17-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:31:40-07:00","id":1130440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130430#post1130430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Eras is just setting material. The only thing of use I've got was meager fleshing out of the Pure. And I mean, meager in the extreme (should've been included in the Corebook). For a game based almost exclusively on antagonists; the game needs to put emphasis on them already.<br /> <br /> Instead we got what, fantastic pregnancy rules and conditions. *eyeroll*</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting material is still <i>material</i> though. &quot;We're getting no material&quot; is a very different argument from &quot;I dislike the material we're getting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pick a goalpost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:36:32-07:00","id":1130442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130428#post1130428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A conversation can have rebuttals.<br /> <br /> I'm a Mummy fan who's also played a lot of Geist. To hear someone feel 'abandoned' when their game has an updated core and its first supplement while these games won't be up to the new edition for at least another year or two feels a little bit oblivious to the state of other gamelines out there, as does the nonsensical &quot;Dark Eras doesn't count as content!&quot; statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit you got a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:38:40-07:00","id":1130444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130412#post1130412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a whopping 10 and soon to be 11 game lines in CofD alone</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wait, what's the 11th? I haven't heard about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:43:50-07:00","id":1130448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130444#post1130444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, what's the 11th? I haven't heard about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant: The Renegades</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130430#post1130430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Eras is just setting material. The only thing of use I've got was meager fleshing out of the Pure. And I mean, meager in the extreme (should've been included in the Corebook). For a game based almost exclusively on antagonists; the game needs to put emphasis on them already.<br /> <br /> Instead we got what, fantastic pregnancy rules and conditions. *eyeroll*</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's just the setting, only the major insipriation a lot of people use for their games. Merely the part of the book that compels people who don't have time to play games too often (like yours truely) to buy books.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I hate it when people use the word &quot;fluff&quot; to describe the setting of a game. That's often the part that is the most compelling and the hardest to write. And yeah, it absolutely counts as being supplements for the game. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, nothing was listed in the brochure for Promethean either, but we know there is a Night Horrors book in the works already, so clearly just because nothing is listed doesn't mean nothing's happening. I sincerely doubt Werewolf has been abandoned or disrespected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-17-2017, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:51:43-07:00","id":1130458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130430#post1130430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Eras is just setting material. The only thing of use I've got was meager fleshing out of the Pure. And I mean, meager in the extreme (should've been included in the Corebook). For a game based almost exclusively on antagonists; the game needs to put emphasis on them already.<br /> <br /> Instead we got what, fantastic pregnancy rules and conditions. *eyeroll*</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry for quoting you, but I think this exemplifies best what I want to talk about.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">Something not being <i>your </i>cup of tea does not make it bad. It just means it is not working for your table. Other lines are not necessarily being favoured just because your favourite doesn't get as much new stuff right now. There may still come a time where your gameline gets more stuff than the others in a certain timeframe, after all, things are being rebooted into 2ed right now. Things like that have happened, and will likely happen again.<br /> </div> You are not the only table, and sometimes, throwing out a seemingly crazy idea is a good call. Some of those will become great things and used, others will wither and die. That is fine. I felt that information added quite some flesh to the Uratha state, though, and will probably make use of it in some plot hooks (for Beast, though).<br /> The sense of entitlement I interpret into these posts (I assume you do not feel entitled to supplement material, and this understanding of mine is due to how I read it) makes me kinda edgy. To me, the Chronicles of Darkness are pretty much a gift. Sure, I pay for the books, but still: there is little out there that intrigues me as much, I like pretty much every gameline and even though I haven't played them all, I enjoy just reading and imagining things with some of them (e.g. Mummy) and the last thing I want to see happen is the diversity collapsing. They are a luxury, a fun pasttime. I don't think that I can make demands for things better suited to my tastes, and I think it is good that this is the case (if that had been the case, we'd probably never gotten Changeling: the Lost, and BOY would that be a loss, wouldn't it ?!)<br /> And seriously, if Stew (was it?) decided that he would rather focus on Apocalypse, that would be sad since I prefer Forsaken by a wide margine, but it would be his call to make. I have no part in that. This reminds me of how people constantly complain about JRR Martin taking ages with his next book, or Patrick Rothfuss still not having released The Doors of Stone, sometimes to the point they insult the author. That kind of whining (I call it that because that is what it reminds me of; no offense meant) that person xy should focus on z, because <i>I </i>like z more than their other projects, would make me as an author want to do less of z. I have no right to z. I am not entitled to z. I am, however, in the lucky position that someone likes creating something that I like (and somehow, manages to get by on that). And personally? I'd rather wait for something done right, than be dissatisfied with something rushed.<br /> I understand this is not the only position one can have, and I understand listening to the fans is a valid concern etc. I do not mean to come across condescending, but I needed to get this off my chest. And just to beat the dead horse, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> already said, Werewolf is in a pretty good state compared to people that wait for a 2ed Core, like us Geist fans. And we in turn are still better off than the Mummy fans...<br /> I for one adore Dark Eras, and think they are a wonderful supplement. For every line.<br /> <br /> I wholeheartedly agree with the statement that there should be more information on antagonists, though. Because stuff like that is always helpful, and nice, and interesting. There is some pretty good homebrew to bridge the time, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:02:47-07:00","id":1130465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130430#post1130430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eras is just setting material. The only thing of use I've got was meager fleshing out of the Pure. And I mean, meager in the extreme (should've been included in the Corebook). For a game based almost exclusively on antagonists; the game needs to put emphasis on them already.<br /> <br /> Instead we got what, fantastic pregnancy rules and conditions. *eyeroll*</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you maybe not roll your eyes at the pregnancy rules? They are (as you put it) fantastic, and parenthood is something the developers (Rose, specifically) have said has been woefully under-represented territory in CofD.<br /> <br /> Anyway, just because you don't like the material werewolf has been getting doesn't mean it hasn't been getting material. Right now Werewolf has the most 2e-relevant material of any CofD game line, save Demon and Vampire. Demon's supplements came primarily from Kickstarter stretch goals, and while Vampire has been getting a fair bit of love lately, it's had to catch up after its own three year dry spell. Meanwhile, Mage is still waiting on its first supplement that started development over a year ago right after Mage 2e came out, Promethean doesn't even have anything planned (unless it's on the Gen Con brochure, I haven't seen it yet), Changeling, Hunter, and Geist aren't even out yet, and Mummy was only just announced to even be <i>getting</i> a second edition. And this is all before taking into account WoD, Exalted, Scion, Trinity, Pugmire, Cavaliers, or Scarred Lands.<br /> <br /> Every line has dry spells. It's a side effect of one company working on over 20 different games simultaneously. Werewolf will have new supplements eventually, and in the meantime, be glad it at least has Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:05:38-07:00","id":1130470,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Promethean does have a Night Horrors book in first drafts, as per the Monday Meeting Notes, but I didn't see it meantioned in the Brochure. Hence why I am entirely unconcerned about Werewolf not getting any new books meantioned in the Brochure either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:14:31-07:00","id":1130472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130448#post1130448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's just the setting, only the major insipriation a lot of people use for their games. Merely the part of the book that compels people who don't have time to play games too often (like yours truely) to buy books.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I hate it when people use the word &quot;fluff&quot; to describe the setting of a game. That's often the part that is the most compelling and the hardest to write. And yeah, it absolutely counts as being supplements for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspirations... for historical games. Which I don't play. Meanwhile we've got crap all on claimed, hosts save some dread powers, etc because, well, setting you guys.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> The other lines dry spells at least had presence in the monday meeting notes. Werewolf have nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:21:51-07:00","id":1130476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130458#post1130458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sorry for quoting you, but I think this exemplifies best what I want to talk about.<br /> <div align=\"center\">Something not being <i>your </i>cup of tea does not make it bad. It just means it is not working for your table. Other lines are not necessarily being favoured just because your favourite doesn't get as much new stuff right now. There may still come a time where your gameline gets more stuff than the others in a certain timeframe, after all, things are being rebooted into 2ed right now. Things like that have happened, and will likely happen again.</div> <br /> You are not the only table, and sometimes, throwing out a seemingly crazy idea is a good call. Some of those will become great things and used, others will wither and die. That is fine. I felt that information added quite some flesh to the Uratha state, though, and will probably make use of it in some plot hooks (for Beast, though).<br /> The sense of entitlement I interpret into these posts (I assume you do not feel entitled to supplement material, and this understanding of mine is due to how I read it) makes me kinda edgy. To me, the Chronicles of Darkness are pretty much a gift. Sure, I pay for the books, but still: there is little out there that intrigues me as much, I like pretty much every gameline and even though I haven't played them all, I enjoy just reading and imagining things with some of them (e.g. Mummy) and the last thing I want to see happen is the diversity collapsing. They are a luxury, a fun pasttime. I don't think that I can make demands for things better suited to my tastes, and I think it is good that this is the case (if that had been the case, we'd probably never gotten Changeling: the Lost, and BOY would that be a loss, wouldn't it ?!)<br /> And seriously, if Stew (was it?) decided that he would rather focus on Apocalypse, that would be sad since I prefer Forsaken by a wide margine, but it would be his call to make. I have no part in that. This reminds me of how people constantly complain about JRR Martin taking ages with his next book, or Patrick Rothfuss still not having released The Doors of Stone, sometimes to the point they insult the author. That kind of whining (I call it that because that is what it reminds me of; no offense meant) that person xy should focus on z, because <i>I </i>like z more than their other projects, would make me as an author want to do less of z. I have no right to z. I am not entitled to z. I am, however, in the lucky position that someone likes creating something that I like (and somehow, manages to get by on that). And personally? I'd rather wait for something done right, than be dissatisfied with something rushed.<br /> I understand this is not the only position one can have, and I understand listening to the fans is a valid concern etc. I do not mean to come across condescending, but I needed to get this off my chest. And just to beat the dead horse, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> already said, Werewolf is in a pretty good state compared to people that wait for a 2ed Core, like us Geist fans. And we in turn are still better off than the Mummy fans...<br /> I for one adore Dark Eras, and think they are a wonderful supplement. For every line.<br /> <br /> I wholeheartedly agree with the statement that there should be more information on antagonists, though. Because stuff like that is always helpful, and nice, and interesting. There is some pretty good homebrew to bridge the time, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not &quot;whining&quot; at the lack of forsaken supplements because &quot;Weee, I want moar books&quot; I want stuff addressing basic concepts of the game that fell by the sidelines because they had to cram a 200 pages supplement in the form of the Idigam Chronicle because our corporate overlords couldn't figure out how to brand their shit for years. (Hell,it's a miracle we ever had tilts in the book, which would have been pretty lame if we didn't cuz Urshul would've sucked then.)<br /> <br /> How old is Mummy? Forsaken has over 10 years of stuff to cover. Mummy has a corebook and two supplements. See the disparity there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-17-2017, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:24:41-07:00","id":1130479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130472#post1130472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inspirations... for historical games. Which I don't play. Meanwhile we've got crap all on claimed, hosts save some dread powers, etc because, well, setting you guys.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> The other lines dry spells at least had presence in the monday meeting notes. Werewolf have nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've used every single Dark Era I can to set up modern games. Hell, Sundered World is the oldest Dark Era and it is potentially the most relevant to modern Werewolf and Mage games. I know that with my Expansion, I'm pushing Crossover Rule hard (although not for Werewolf) and I suspect the other four expansion backers will do the same.<br /> <br /> Just because you don't like them, you don't find them useful, and you haven't found a way to use them in modern games does not mean other people haven't. If you don't like it, that's fine. Other people are content as a cucumber to get more setting. We disagree and nothing stops us from agreeing to disagree. Feel free to lobby to Rich and Stew to make more Werewolf content along the lines you want to see.<br /> <br /> But don't try to claim that there's been no support. And don't try to claim that the setting material doesn't count just because you don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:25:33-07:00","id":1130480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130440#post1130440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick a goalpost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, i want more mechanics material instead of Dark eras book with limited applications. There are tons of gifts and rites that need conversions.<br /> <br /> Fluffy history books are nice and all but ultimately incredible limited in usefulness for a game unless you happen to wanna run a game in the period stated.<br /> <br /> An example is lines like &quot;Uratha might go into the shadows in search of rare/forgotten rituals&quot; and then having a minimal selection of rituals and none who can be considered &quot;rare/forgotten&quot;. Or &quot;tribes can help you teach you tribal secrets for certain preys&quot; and then finding out that constitute exactly 1 ritual per tribe with limited utility to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130423#post1130423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably one of the reasons mage is so popular is that Dave had gone to such lengths to talk about it, including talking about things that aren't in books and might never be in books.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNot only that, mage is a pretty complete rulebook that Forsaken isnt. You got material to play mostly everything you need barring some very niche mechanics (and even then those mechanics were mentioned in the next supplement). You got the special powers to the seers and all.<br /> <br /> Now Werewolf, of the 6 (humans, Host, Claimed, Spirits, werewolves, Idigam) antagonist and keep in mind that unlike mage the game revolves around hunting this 6 beings so rules for them should be present. What we got? Human covered in the Chrod, Host we are given 2 example of host and little else. Spirits we got less info than the 1st edition core (thank god i didnt sold my copy) and long needed clarification even after 2 books (1st Core and predators) is still missing. Claimed we got info but werewolves? We got jack-shit on the Pure, we had to wait for a blog post or dark eras to even get their hunt benefit and we still missing their gifts.<br /> <br /> As to having 1 supplement, honestly is a very underwhelming one. First chapter is example of very particular packs and how they function so unless i wanna run a all-firemen pack, or Wolf blooded and 3 Uratha packs or IT company pack is pretty useless. Yeah i get it the definition of pack is more loose now, you dont need to waste one entire chapter of the book on it.<br /> <br /> Chapter 2 is optional rules that might or might not be useful depending on your game.<br /> <br /> Then next chapter is actually useful with a system for lodges. Problem is that we dont get any guide for the main bonus of a lodge. And thats just a part of the chapter.<br /> <br /> And finally chapter 4 is another, &quot;blurbs about settings too incomplete to be useful&quot;, it was a somewhat useless chapter in the Core but now is completely useless, unless you wanna run those places and you happen to dig their setup.<br /> <br /> I get it, fluff books are easier to do. They dont require playtesting and as much effort as writing mechanics. But this is the main reason people chalk the Dark Eras books as &quot;not counting&quot; because is just fluff after fluff with such limited usefulness.<br /> <br /> But honestly i feel the company is expecting me to play game designer for them and they just wanna be novelist. Dark Eras 2 is the straw that broke the camel for me, i wont give OPP a cent for yet another useless fluff book (unless the aforementioned conditions are meet).<br /> <br /> First Dark Eras got 3 times its needed budget but Dark Eras 2 barely managed to reach 1/2 more of it needed budget and i hope is because people are getting tired of the general attitude of just putting more empty of mechanics fluff books.<br /> <br /> Instead of concentrating on the lines they already have OPP keeps releasing new ones and leaving the previous ones to rot. Instead of getting Geist 2nd or even mummy we got beast (and we all know how that one turn up) and now Deviant. Instead of getting Forsaken books that we need, we got yet another Dark eras.<br /> <br /> Honestly if we got all the conversion of the gifts, the clarifications on certain iffy rules and maybe even rites then i wouldnt even mind if the gamelines is forgotten under a pile between Dark eras mage: 1902 and Dark eras Promethean: 1903. Even in the case of mage, Signs of Sorcery is out and i am done because it is all i need to play but not even that.<br /> <br /> <br /> QUICK EDIT: Because i know someone is gonna jump the gun on this, because they always jump the gun on this kind of things. I am not saying that fluffy book like dark eras are entirely without merit or usefulness but that they are of very very limited usefulness because unless your game is gonna run in that exact same time period or place, and the take of the author mesh with yours then its isnt of much use. On the other hand a gift or rite, mechanics for host is useful and applicable no matter when and where i run the game (barring that the concept of the gift in question doesnt exist at the time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Typo 08-17-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:36:34-07:00","id":1130488,"title":"","content":"I'd sooner see five more Dark Eras books than one that was just page after page of Rites and enemy writeups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:36:54-07:00","id":1130489,"title":"","content":"1) Thanks for picking a goal post.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Fluff&quot; books are not fucking easy. <i>Historical</i> &quot;fluff&quot; books are <i>really</i> not fucking easy. Kindly do not dismiss the hard work that goes into it.<br /> <br /> You find it useless, sure, okay. You don't consider it important, fine, okay. You wanna argue about the business practice, really, go ahead.<br /> <br /> But don't make it out like this is cruise control work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:37:00-07:00","id":1130490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130480#post1130480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of getting Geist 2nd or even mummy we got beast (and we all know how that one turn up)..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I won't object other arguments since I'm not the one that should tell you how to feel, but I also won't say nothing if you state things that aren't true. Enough with the &quot;Beast was a disaster everyone hates&quot; meme. And Deviant seems great. Easy to say the books you don't like are wasted paper.<br /> <br /> Before going forward, keep in mind that my favorite lines are Werewolf, Promethean, Geist, Mummy and Beast. Geist since I discovered the CoD and Book Of The Dead was (and still is) the only separate supplement we got so far. It's not like I don't get the desire to have more stuff, but come on, there's criticism and there's finding more faults than those that are actually there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:39:16-07:00","id":1130491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130476#post1130476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not &quot;whining&quot; at the lack of forsaken supplements because &quot;Weee, I want moar books&quot; I want stuff addressing basic concepts of the game that fell by the sidelines because they had to cram a 200 pages supplement in the form of the Idigam Chronicle because our corporate overlords couldn't figure out how to brand their shit for years.<br /> <br /> How old is Mummy? Forsaken has over 10 years of stuff to cover. Mummy has a corebook and two supplements. See the disparity there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically stated that I do not consider you to be whining, but that this reminds me of whining. I do not blame people for things that I understand, unless I am very sure that is what they meant me to understand.<br /> <br /> Mummy does not even have a Core yet. So playing 2ed is rather hard, what with having to converse the given old material to 2ed from scratch, whereas a makeshift workaround with the given 2ed Core and old material is a lot easier. See the disparity there?<br /> <br /> People love setting information, because it helps them come up with their own stuff - ChroD has traditionally been very sandbox, and no one stops you from using your imagination to make up a few Claimed etc. I pointed towards homebrew for Claimed etc, because there is a HUGE amount of things you could draw on. We are currently playing a chronicle with Zhibesi, and it is awesome! I would like more basic concepts, because I always do, but I do not think more enemy information is what is needed to play the game - at least, not the way I play. I am sorry if you can't play the way you want to (being sincere here, I know those feels).<br /> <br /> Still, I want to point to my former post again because you just complained about <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inspirations... for historical games. Which I don't play. </div> </div> </div>. Sometimes you just don't get what you want, a lot of people are pretty happy with what was given. <br /> <br /> I ain't denying that you can grieve the fact there is not enough stuff for you to play the way you want to - but claiming the gameline is abandoned when 2nd Ed is pretty much <i>all </i>a work in progress seems hasty to me. Especially if you are aware the same developer might be a bit stretched. Patience. I am sure the next supplement that will come out will have stuff you are interested in! Because I am optimistic like that sometimes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:45:55-07:00","id":1130499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130448#post1130448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason I hate it when people use the word &quot;fluff&quot; to describe the setting of a game. That's often the part that is the most compelling and the hardest to write. And yeah, it absolutely counts as being supplements for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay i have to ask, how is more difficult to written setting than mechanics? I am honestly curious, because mechanics require to make them compelling and require tons of playtesting. Fluff however dont. If we were talking about the city books, i could get it because its tons of npcs and factions that interact with each other and they are hard to pull off right (Denver being the only good one i have read) but things like the city blurb in the new cores? How are they more difficult to write than mechanics? They are basically a little plot seed with little to no explanation or depth to them. They seems more like elevators pitches than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:47:45-07:00","id":1130502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130489#post1130489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Thanks for picking a goal post.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Fluff&quot; books are not fucking easy. <i>Historical</i> &quot;fluff&quot; books are <i>really</i> not fucking easy. Kindly do not dismiss the hard work that goes into it.<br /> <br /> You find it useless, sure, okay. You don't consider it important, fine, okay. You wanna argue about the business practice, really, go ahead.<br /> <br /> But don't make it out like this is cruise control work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is exactly why I don't like the term &quot;fluff.&quot; It has the connotation of the writing either being light and easy, or insubstantial and meaningless. I love crunchy games, I gleefully backed O.L.D. is N.E.W., but I have hard copies of every 2e core rulebook for precisely one game: Chronicles of Darkness. That would NEVER have happened if it weren't for the brilliant writing of the game's setting. The fact that W:tF 2e's setting was so much more evocative and digestible than 1e is why it is one of my favourite games when I could not give a fuck about 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:58:37-07:00","id":1130513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130499#post1130499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay i have to ask, how is more difficult to written setting than mechanics? I am honestly curious, because mechanics require to make them compelling and require tons of playtesting. Fluff however dont. If we were talking about the city books, i could get it because its tons of npcs and factions that interact with each other and they are hard to pull off right (Denver being the only good one i have read) but things like the city blurb in the new cores? How are they more difficult to write than mechanics? They are basically a little plot seed with little to no explanation or depth to them. They seems more like elevators pitches than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For designing mechanic you need testing, like you said. But for designing setting you need research which is a process that is at least as involved as the testing of mechanics. <br /> Easy access to the internet has given the impression that knowledge can be easily found, but the truth is that internet or no internet you still need to go through extensive research which takes not only time, but also judgment for when you find informations that contradict one another or when there are multiple schools of thoughts.<br /> Take in mind that is only when you want to end up with 'fluff' and setting of quality. With poor research you end up with Set, you know, the god of snakes and darkness.<br /> <br /> Really this is why i'm liking the development of Scion so much. The team shows that they will not scrimp on the research. Doing research is showing respect for the material.<br /> <br /> Anyway i hope i've explained things well enough. (i'm not the best at writing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:00:13-07:00","id":1130515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130499#post1130499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay i have to ask, how is more difficult to written setting than mechanics? I am honestly curious, because mechanics require to make them compelling and require tons of playtesting. Fluff however dont. If we were talking about the city books, i could get it because its tons of npcs and factions that interact with each other and they are hard to pull off right (Denver being the only good one i have read) but things like the city blurb in the new cores? How are they more difficult to write than mechanics? They are basically a little plot seed with little to no explanation or depth to them. They seems more like elevators pitches than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question and fair question. From my own experience (strictly not as a game writer/designer/developer). I find writing a monster in the CR 25-30 range for Pathfinder to be easier than writing compelling fiction. I have examples that I can work from, I can do the math to figure out statistically how often it can do damage, and I can ballpark the range that something should fall in to be balanced.<br /> <br /> Writing compelling fiction, on the other hand, I find challenging. Predicting what will resonate with people, covering my bases for plotholes, making something compelling, leaving interesting plothooks for people to grab on to... its hard work. I spend so much time editing and second guessing my own work, even for short flash fiction. Sometimes the stuff that I think is awesome barely gets any attention, while the stuff that I run off in 15 minutes gets tons of appreciation. The only think that I can do to try and improve myself is keep writing more and more and more. There's no standard curve for it.<br /> <br /> Here's the analogy I use. Crunch is linear in difficulty. It boils down to math. You can easily predict it if you know the rules and you've done enough practice.<br /> <br /> Setting involves more human interaction. You have to speak to your reader in a greater way than you do mechanically. Because of the human element, it is quadratic. The learning curve is much, much steeper. Historical setting hits you with the additional whammy of having to do research, much of which is contradictory, and can easily blow your plans to shit.<br /> <br /> In my opinion: setting is much, much harder to write.<br /> <br /> <u><b>EDIT: </b></u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130513#post1130513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For designing mechanic you need testing, like you said. But for designing setting you need research which is a process that is at least as involved as the testing of mechanics.<br /> Easy access to the internet has given the impression that knowledge can be easily found, but the truth is that internet or no internet you still need to go through extensive research which takes not only time, but also judgment for when you find informations that contradict one another or when there are multiple schools of thoughts.<br /> Take in mind that is only when you want to end up with 'fluff' and setting of quality. With poor research you end up with Set, you know, the god of snakes and darkness.<br /> <br /> Really this is why i'm liking the development of Scion so much. The team shows that they will not scrimp on the research. Doing research is showing respect for the material.<br /> <br /> Anyway i hope i've explained things well enough. (i'm not the best at writing)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent way of phrasing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:00:48-07:00","id":1130516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130489#post1130489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Thanks for picking a goal post.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Fluff&quot; books are not fucking easy. <i>Historical</i> &quot;fluff&quot; books are <i>really</i> not fucking easy. Kindly do not dismiss the hard work that goes into it.<br /> <br /> You find it useless, sure, okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah my bad, it was a typo. It should have said &quot;they are easier to make&quot; instead of easy to make. Big difference. Both arent easy to make but i honestly believe that fluff is easier to write than mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130488#post1130488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd sooner see five more Dark Eras books than one that was just page after page of Rites and enemy writeups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a oversimplification of what i said. I dont necesarily mean a only mechanics book (thought i would love that) but instead of the 5 dark eras book what about 1 book with the clarifications on influence + some rites that are actually rare (or remove the lines) + the actual rules updates on Pure gifts. Things people actually need to run the game. If we got all that and then got all the 1999 dark eras books, then fine. But when we are missing material to run the actual game thats kind of a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130490#post1130490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't object other arguments since I'm not the one that should tell you how to feel, but I also won't say nothing if you state things that aren't true. Enough with the &quot;Beast was a disaster everyone hates&quot; meme. And Deviant seems great. Easy to say the books you don't like are wasted paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont particularly hate Deviant since it isnt out yet but my point is more that OPP seems to be chasing the next big thing instead of caring for the lines they got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:01:04-07:00","id":1130517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130448#post1130448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/deviant-deviant-the-renegades/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant: The Renegades</a><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Already have an idea for a super soldier who's been spliced with ant DNA. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:02:51-07:00","id":1130519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130517#post1130517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice! Already have an idea for a super soldier who's been spliced with ant DNA. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Psshh... fly DNA or bust! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:10:00-07:00","id":1130525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130499#post1130499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay i have to ask, how is more difficult to written setting than mechanics? I am honestly curious, because mechanics require to make them compelling and require tons of playtesting. Fluff however dont. If we were talking about the city books, i could get it because its tons of npcs and factions that interact with each other and they are hard to pull off right (Denver being the only good one i have read) but things like the city blurb in the new cores? How are they more difficult to write than mechanics? They are basically a little plot seed with little to no explanation or depth to them. They seems more like elevators pitches than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>A power simply has to work on it's own terms. Most material of this sort aren't tested outside of cores and more just rationally double-checked.<br /> <br /> Setting has to mesh with what's been established while expanding the setting in ways that are interesting and generate conversation, and it has to be written well.<br /> <br /> What's more, most of the money-making audience is in for exactly this stuff-if mechanics are a little sloppy, oh well, but if the setting goes wonky, LORD HELP YOU.(Most payers do not actually play the game, and instead enjoy these games as basically open fiction and daydream spaces)<br /> <br /> And if you're doing historical setting, not only do you have to get your fantasy to mesh with reality, but you have research the <i>fuck</i> out of the time period to make sure you get things right, because if you don't, not only do you risk turning away your history loving crowd(larger than you'd think), but you also run risks of horribly making light of real lives. And on top of that, you have to balance that accuracy with the needs of play, of how much of what on each side has to go out.<br /> <br /> Mechanics are stupid simple once you've found something fun to play with, and they are inherently easier to fiddle with-the knobs, at least, are all labeled. Setting-setting is a <i>bitch</i> to write.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, consider-writers currently only get paid for the words used in the end(that might change, who knows). Writers and devs don't get paid for the amount of time put into research and revision that goes on. Between the two, mechanics usually end up requiring less research and revision than setting.*<br /> <br /> *Obvious exceptions includes the developer's work into the initial systems-consider this post primarily focused on supplements. And even then, setting STILL is just as arduous, and can still be more so depending on the nature of that setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:16:03-07:00","id":1130529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130515#post1130515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question and fair question. From my own experience (strictly not as a game writer/designer/developer). I find writing a monster in the CR 25-30 range for Pathfinder to be easier than writing compelling fiction. I have examples that I can work from, I can do the math to figure out statistically how often it can do damage, and I can ballpark the range that something should fall in to be balanced.<br /> <br /> Writing compelling fiction, on the other hand, I find challenging. Predicting what will resonate with people, covering my bases for plotholes, making something compelling, leaving interesting plothooks for people to grab on to... its hard work. I spend so much time editing and second guessing my own work, even for short flash fiction. Sometimes the stuff that I think is awesome barely gets any attention, while the stuff that I run off in 15 minutes gets tons of appreciation. The only think that I can do to try and improve myself is keep writing more and more and more. There's no standard curve for it.<br /> <br /> Here's the analogy I use. Crunch is linear in difficulty. It boils down to math. You can easily predict it if you know the rules and you've done enough practice.<br /> <br /> Setting involves more human interaction. You have to speak to your reader in a greater way than you do mechanically. Because of the human element, it is quadratic. The learning curve is much, much steeper. Historical setting hits you with the additional whammy of having to do research, much of which is contradictory, and can easily blow your plans to shit.<br /> <br /> In my opinion: setting is much, much harder to write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an interesting point, i have experience it the other way around. With mechanics for werewolf specially difficult to think about, convert and second guessing or needing (and lacking) a second set of trusting eyes. One mistake and i get a broken mechanic too powerful to use. I experience the same with rites, which rites should be converted? Social rites are definetely a no because they are a holdover from Apocalypse but what about those that function similar to lunar gifts? Should be included? Shouldnt be? Or those that deal aggravated damage? Or do something already covered by another gift?<br /> <br /> Worse for gifts, the common dev wisdom is that they are the equivalent of a rank 3 from 1st edition but power level in 1st was all over the place with some being very powerful and some not even worth it. Same feeling that you got with Fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130513#post1130513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For designing mechanic you need testing, like you said. But for designing setting you need research which is a process that is at least as involved as the testing of mechanics.<br /> Easy access to the internet has given the impression that knowledge can be easily found, but the truth is that internet or no internet you still need to go through extensive research which takes not only time, but also judgment for when you find informations that contradict one another or when there are multiple schools of thoughts.<br /> Take in mind that is only when you want to end up with 'fluff' and setting of quality. With poor research you end up with Set, you know, the god of snakes and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe is because i have had to write many research papers, investigations for work and do write setting from the ground up that it seems easier to me or at least i dont face as much problem as i do with mechanics. Or maybe because i process fluff books on a personal level more mechanically than by feeling. For example i never like &quot;unique&quot; cities for the lines (boston, Miami, new orleans), the reason i like Denver so much is that is very generic and by the number covering each antagonist in equal measure. Kinda &quot;Vanilla Werewolf&quot; which to me is what a 1st city book should be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130525#post1130525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A power simply has to work on it's own terms. Most material of this sort aren't tested outside of cores and more just rationally double-checked.<br /> <br /> What's more, most of the money-making audience is in for exactly this stuff-if mechanics are a little sloppy, oh well, but if the setting goes wonky, LORD HELP YOU.(Most payers do not actually play the game, and instead enjoy these games as basically open fiction and daydream spaces)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats incredible disheartening to read. I am so depressed right now. But thanks for the clarification guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:24:54-07:00","id":1130534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130529#post1130529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats incredible disheartening to read. I am so depressed right now. But thanks for the clarification guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm...not quite sure why that would be the case. But glad to help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:31:50-07:00","id":1130541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130525#post1130525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's more, most of the money-making audience is in for exactly this stuff-if mechanics are a little sloppy, oh well, but if the setting goes wonky, LORD HELP YOU.(Most payers do not actually play the game, and instead enjoy these games as basically open fiction and daydream spaces)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just ask to the Exalted forum about 2nd Edition and its contributions about the setting. They'll give you enough proof to support this thesis until the end of times (does not help that it was not perfect even on the mechanics side, but people down there burst into flames when you talk about some of the fluff of 2nd Edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:40:54-07:00","id":1130548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130529#post1130529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe is because i have had to write many research papers, investigations for work and do write setting from the ground up that it seems easier to me or at least i dont face as much problem as i do with mechanics. Or maybe because i process fluff books on a personal level more mechanically than by feeling. For example i never like &quot;unique&quot; cities for the lines (boston, Miami, new orleans), the reason i like Denver so much is that is very generic and by the number covering each antagonist in equal measure. Kinda &quot;Vanilla Werewolf&quot; which to me is what a 1st city book should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I feel the exact opposite of you. Because of how many research papers I've written, I feel like I have to do more research, double check more facts, and consider more options because I want my work to feel genuine, especially to people familar with the settings. And I love the unique and decidedly not generic settings. They show me ways that I can create something unique, they hone in on themes, and they feel like they are part of living, breathing world. <br /> <br /> I think we just have very different tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:42:22-07:00","id":1130550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130541#post1130541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ask to the Exalted forum about 2nd Edition and its contributions about the setting. They'll give you enough proof to support this thesis until the end of times (does not help that it was not perfect even on the mechanics side, but people down there burst into flames when you talk about some of the fluff of 2nd Edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't even have to go as far as that. Pick a gameline in Chronicles and look where the conversations are.<br /> <br /> As a minor example, Electroshock Therapy was this big ol' overpowered cheese thing in Promethean the Created. I literally never heard of it until some point in Second Edition's development. Wanna know what I did hear about? Transhumanism in Promethean.<br /> <br /> Mechanics are cool, and having good mechanics is integral to making a game setting work-but that's the catch, people play in the setting using the mechanics, at least in games like this. These are setting first games-and if you compare them to games that are, ideologically, more &quot;people play with the mechanics using a setting&quot;, they sell better.<br /> <br /> I do want to reiterate a addendum to the earlier post, because I'm setting up pieces to start working on my own game-a lot of what I've said does get blurred with the initial creation of a thing, because mechanical and setting bedrock is a thing to build and it can be hard to really build a good game at that point, mechanically speaking, particularly since you really have to marry it to the setting. But as time goes on and the mechanical sense of things is figured out enough to be that bedrock, setting becomes way harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:48:18-07:00","id":1130554,"title":"","content":"If &quot;crunch&quot; (god I hate the term) is more important to you than setting, Chronicles of Darkness is probably not the right game for you. Not because the mechanics aren't good, but because your priorities are very different than those of the people producing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:56:24-07:00","id":1130557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130554#post1130554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &quot;crunch&quot; (god I hate the term) is more important to you than setting, Chronicles of Darkness is probably not the right game for you. Not because the mechanics aren't good, but because your priorities are very different than those of the people producing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was about to say:<br /> <br /> Wasn't the primary hook/point of CofD to be the setting, mythos, and story surrounding the gamelines and not the mechanics? And that even if you did want more mechanics, because of the toolbox nature of CofD, the game actively encourages players and STs to come up with stuff themselves?<br /> <br /> Otherwise if I'd wanted to bumble with mechanics more, I'd just whip out Pathfinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:56:27-07:00","id":1130558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130554#post1130554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &amp;quot;crunch&amp;quot; (god I hate the term) is more important to you than setting, Chronicles of Darkness is probably not the right game for you. Not because the mechanics aren't good, but because your priorities are very different than those of the people producing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How come my storytelling game isn't prioritizing mechanical complexity!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:04:25-07:00","id":1130561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130557#post1130557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I was about to say:<br /> <br /> Wasn't the primary hook/point of CofD to be the setting, mythos, and story surrounding the gamelines and not the mechanics? And that even if you did want more mechanics, because of the toolbox nature of CofD, the game actively encourages players and STs to come up with stuff themselves?<br /> <br /> Otherwise if I'd wanted to bumble with mechanics more, I'd just whip out Pathfinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't want to bring up the toolbox thing cause I already know what the response to that will be. And honestly, it's not even an unfair response. But if you are the type to think of &quot;fluff&quot; and &quot;crunch&quot; as two different things, you're not thinking of games the same way CofD's developers do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:18:30-07:00","id":1130568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130548#post1130548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I love the unique and decidedly not generic settings. They show me ways that I can create something unique, they hone in on themes, and they feel like they are part of living, breathing world.<br /> <br /> I think we just have very different tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a matter of time and place to me. Personally i believe the first city book of a line (or in the case of the old core, the example city) should be the most generic one. The sorta-tag line of NWoD was that is a tool box and each city didnt need to conform to form but one, as dm, need to deeply understand the norm before changing it. See how and why each piece fit and understand them before start messing with it.<br /> <br /> Saying this changeling city is different/original because the summer court dominates all year around doesnt have the same weight if i dont understand how and why a city normally function beyond the blurb and white room of the setting description in the book.<br /> <br /> Past the first city book then sure, go nuts. Make a city which its king/prince is decided by lottery.<br /> <br /> On the same vein on time and place, should all the dark eras books had been release around 2012 when all the lines were more or less done. The main 3 had all the mechanics need, same as hunter and changeling. Then I would love 3, 4 or even 5 Dark Eras book. Because they supplements to add to robust main lines.<br /> <br /> Just taking forsaken, one had the Pure and their gifts. Plethora of gifts, Rites and lodges. Lunar gifts, alternative lunar gifts and a System for Antagonist (if the spirits still were clunky). It was a complete line and the Dark eras then would have been the cream and cherry on top of an good pie. But now it feels that the cream and cherry is going into a half baked pie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130550#post1130550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics are cool, and having good mechanics is integral to making a game setting work-but that's the catch, people play in the setting using the mechanics, at least in games like this. These are setting first games-and if you compare them to games that are, ideologically, more &quot;people play with the mechanics using a setting&quot;, they sell better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will point out that there is a difference between universal applicable fluff and fluff of limited use. For example, as we are in werewolf lets keep on werewolf, the tactic and life of the pure is pretty universal. How tribes teach and convince newly change uratha to join the forsaken is pretty universal. How spirit teach gifts and why, is pretty universal.<br /> <br /> Dark eras book and location blurb arent, of all the times presented, which one as a DM i am gonna use? The crossovers one present the question of &quot;do i wanna put X splat in my game?&quot; and even those that are uni-splat, the question remains of whether i wanna run this splat game in this time and place? Because how Uratha society function in say chicago during the prohibition era would really not affect what is going with my game is Seattle 2005.<br /> <br /> Its not even a question of fluff vs Mechanics. Its more of question of a fluff with a very specific use vs mechanics.<br /> <br /> Also the comparison with pathfinder is pretty dishonest. Yes, wod is general like to thinks is very rules light (even thought NWoD has as many rules as 3.5 by its end) but i am not talking about incredible specific mechanics like &quot;specific rules to blow a building using c4 that allows me to calculate the amount needed by the pound&quot; or &quot;a whole system to represent the different schools of Kendo&quot; but instead. Forsaken is a game about hunting 6 preys, why are we missing rules for 2 and half of them? Is not even creating said rules, just updating them to 2nd edition. The argument of &quot;wod isnt about mechanics&quot; doesnt really fly on this because this mechanics existed in 1st<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130557#post1130557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that even if you did want more mechanics, because of the toolbox nature of CofD, the game actively encourages players and STs to come up with stuff themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really the toolbox approach was more on the setting side. &quot;No more metaplot to &quot;limit you&quot;&quot; they said, each city and clan/tribe/etc can be compose of whatever you want.....because we couldnt do that before.....for some reason.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it isnt that much of a toolbox. If it was we would have gotten a chapter on how to create gifts, which we dont have. Or a chapter on how to create Host which i argue is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-17-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:27:41-07:00","id":1130576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130568#post1130568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will point out that there is a difference between universal applicable fluff and fluff of limited use. For example, as we are in werewolf lets keep on werewolf, the tactic and life of the pure is pretty universal. How tribes teach and convince newly change uratha to join the forsaken is pretty universal. How spirit teach gifts and why, is pretty universal.<br /> <br /> Dark eras book and location blurb arent, of all the times presented, which one as a DM i am gonna use? The crossovers one present the question of &quot;do i wanna put X splat in my game?&quot; and even those that are uni-splat, the question remains of whether i wanna run this splat game in this time and place? Because how Uratha society function in say chicago during the prohibition era would really not affect what is going with my game is Seattle 2005.<br /> <br /> Its not even a question of fluff vs Mechanics. Its more of question of a fluff with a very specific use vs mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes into the question of how fluff is used. A minor example on that point is that even if I don't play Mage Noir, reading it gives me a very solid sense of particulars about how American Mages are in modern culture, particularly since I do love have old-timers in my settings. Lily, Sabre and Thorn very directly influenced the Paris setting I wrote, as another example. But that may not be how others play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-17-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:29:27-07:00","id":1130578,"title":"","content":"We literally got a free blog post on how to make Gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:33:14-07:00","id":1130580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130576#post1130576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes into the question of how fluff is used. A minor example on that point is that even if I don't Mage Noir, reading it gives me a very solid sense of particulars about how American Mages are in modern culture, particularly since I do love have old-timers in my settings. Lily, Sabre and Thorn very directly influenced the Paris setting I wrote, as another example. But that may not be how others play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got WAY more out of Sundered World than I did out of The Pack. And that's not a knock against The Pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:37:52-07:00","id":1130583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130580#post1130580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got WAY more out of Sundered World than I did out of The Pack. And that's not a knock against The Pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an interesting comparison in use. I love both, but I would necessarily use The Pack* more than Sundered World-BUT Sundered World is always going to inform a lot of aspects in regards to how I handle the big picture and several mysteries I'd have as settings for Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But then again, some people <i>wouldn't</i>. And that's fine.<br /> <br /> *Mind you, I consider The Pack to be my second favorite Forsaken Supplement, following Blood of the Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:38:23-07:00","id":1130584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130554#post1130554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &quot;crunch&quot; (god I hate the term) is more important to you than setting, Chronicles of Darkness is probably not the right game for you. Not because the mechanics aren't good, but because your priorities are very different than those of the people producing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then give us the setting on Bale Hounds, Pure, Hosts, and Claimed beyond a couple of sheet examples. Is that too much to ask? Apparently, since we're not gonna see anything reminiscing that in all of 2017, or 2018.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:41:17-07:00","id":1130586,"title":"","content":"Great job.<br /> <br /> A better 'goalpost' would be a book. A supplement for the game line. Something that answers the questions the core book and Pack left up in the air. You can include Dark Eras for werewolf if you like, but since it has every line in it it doesn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> Vampire's got three, and based on the brochure, one more planned, Guide to the Night. Mage only has Signs of Sorcery, but it also has Tome of the Pentacle in the running.<br /> <br /> Geist and Mummy and other games don't even have a second edition, but they have at least been announced and one is in development. If they're like most other lines, they're going to come out with two books planned. The trend seems to be having a Night Horrors book and some sort of player or Storyteller guide, which is what Beast and Promethean are aiming for, though Beast also has both a Player and Storyteller guide, and Changeling may or may not have its 'The Hedge' book but I'm sure more is planned.<br /> <br /> Back in 2015, a 'Secrets of the Tribes' was teased, but we were told by the writers they haven't heard anything of it, it hasn't appeared on the Monday Meeting blogs, and the developer hasn't mentioned it, or anything.<br /> <br /> Put simply. We know the future of other lines. They have books coming. All of them.<br /> <br /> What is the future of Werewolf the Forsaken? Because while I may not agree with everything LokiRavenSpeak says, based purely on his posts it's easy to tell the game needs more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:47:07-07:00","id":1130588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130584#post1130584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then give us the setting on Bale Hounds, Pure, Hosts, and Claimed beyond a couple of sheet examples. Is that too much to ask? Apparently, since we're not gonna see anything reminiscing that in all of 2017, or 2018.</div> </div> </div> </div>Antagonist books don't seem to really be <i>a thing</i> in second edition, at least not so far. Heck, Vampire currently has the most 2e material after Demon, and we've still seen not one word on Belial's Brood. &quot;Here's a few examples you can use to inform your own antagonist designs&quot; seems to be the direction 2e is headed, which is fine by me. Especially if I accept your premise that we're getting stuff like the pregnancy rules in place of more stat blocks, which are pretty trivial for me to whip up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:50:14-07:00","id":1130590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130588#post1130588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antagonist books don't seem to really be <i>a thing</i> in second edition, at least not so far. Heck, Vampire currently has the most 2e material after Demon, and we've still seen not one word on Belial's Brood. &quot;Here's a few examples you can use to inform your own antagonist designs&quot; seems to be the direction 2e is headed, which is fine by me. Especially if I accept your premise that we're getting stuff like the pregnancy rules in place of more stat blocks, which are pretty trivial for me to whip up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be for the most part because Belial's Brood has taken a diminished role in second edition.<br /> <br /> Beast, Promethean, Demon, all have Night Horrors books in some stage of development, in one just out and published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:50:17-07:00","id":1130591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130561#post1130561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you are the type to think of &quot;fluff&quot; and &quot;crunch&quot; as two different things, you're not thinking of games the same way CofD's developers do.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Alternatively thinking with that distinction can also mean you understand how insanely valuable reflavouring things can be and remember that CofD is a toolbox?<br /> <br /> Also... considering how Clanbooks and Secrets of the Covenants are formatted, Onyx Path must understand that fluff and crunch are two different things...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-17-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:50:52-07:00","id":1130593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130586#post1130586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great job.<br /> <br /> A better 'goalpost' would be a book. A supplement for the game line. You can include Dark Eras for werewolf if you like, but since it has every line in it it doesn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> Vampire's got three, and based on the brochure, one more planned, Guide to the Night. Mage only has Signs of Sorcery, but it also has Tome of the Pentacle in the running.<br /> <br /> Geist and Mummy and other games don't even have a second edition, but they have at least been announced and one is in development. If they're like most other lines, they're going to come out with two books planned. The trend seems to be having a Night Horrors book and some sort of player or Storyteller guide, which is what Beast and Promethean are aiming for, though Beast also has both a Player and Storyteller guide, and Changeling may or may not have its 'The Hedge' book but I'm sure more is planned.<br /> <br /> Back in 2015, a 'Secrets of the Tribes' was teased, but we were told by the writers they haven't heard anything of it, it hasn't appeared on the Monday Meeting blogs, and the developer hasn't mentioned it, or anything.<br /> <br /> Put simply. We know the future of other lines. They have books coming. All of them.<br /> <br /> What is the future of Werewolf the Forsaken? Because while I may not agree with everything LokiRavenSpeak says, based purely on his posts it's easy to tell the game needs more.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll get more books in time. Every line seems to have dry spells and wet spells. Werewolf got a wet spell early in its 2e run and its current dry spell does look to be a long one. But the rain will come again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:01:23-07:00","id":1130599,"title":"","content":"Mind you that a significant factor of the design is to work primarily towards getting out new material and bringing updated old stuff in as a bonus if it can work. Mostly because just releasing whole supplements of &quot;Oh, you've read this before, but now it's updated&quot; is kind of a boring point.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that there is currently the bigger focus on getting all of the lines at least updated, and a lot of manpower is going into that aspect, as well as ensuring that newer lines at least have solid enough support that letting them stand for a while is not going to cause them to wither.<br /> <br /> Now, are these management choices effective on the grand scale? Dunno, and on a customer basis they aren't things I worry about. If others have an issue with that, well, eh. I can see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:40:40-07:00","id":1130615,"title":"","content":"I do think it one things which helps the &quot;we don't really want to rerelease things you have already bought&quot; is the increased focus on dread powers for so many enemy types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:38:34-07:00","id":1130638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130578#post1130578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We literally got a free blog post on how to make Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I already posted my issues with the blogpost and how it isnt a solution for creating gifts. As a blogpost made by the author is fine, i like it. However as a replacement for gifts that are missing is lacking. Problem is that the idea seems all gifts should be equivalent to a rank 3 from 1st edition. Problem is that power level was all over the place with some being extremely powerful and other pretty weak.<br /> <br /> You got ranks 3 gifts that gave you silver claws, other that allows you to walk on smoke and another gave you a +2 to all out attacks. Even the rules set on the guidelines arent followed on the game. Rahu gift overlaps with Strenght ones.<br /> <br /> 2nd Stat boost gifts sometimes got you a +equal to renown, other equals to success and other just reduce the number of successes nescesary for Exceptional.<br /> <br /> Powerlevel also is kinda weird in second edition. 1st was giving aggravated damage like it was candy but now nothing (powers) gives you aggravated but everything else was balanced upwards on power level.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130586#post1130586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great job.<br /> A better 'goalpost' would be a book. A supplement for the game line. Something that answers the questions the core book and Pack left up in the air. You can include Dark Eras for werewolf if you like, but since it has every line in it it doesn't make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is while Chrod normally moves away from antagonist books, in the case of forsaken they should make an exception. The hunt is so much part of Forsaken that an antagonist book is needed.<br /> <br /> It is as if they had released Awakening and 4 arcanums werent in the book. Also if they wanna make the thematic naming, we got &quot;The pack&quot; and the next one should be &quot;The prey&quot;. You dont get more thematic than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130588#post1130588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially if I accept your premise that we're getting stuff like the pregnancy rules in place of more stat blocks, which are pretty trivial for me to whip up.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by stat blocks? Because i am not saying Forsaken need more stated enemies, like &quot;this is redstick, he is a pure. Here is his stats&quot; but instead. Hey here is the kind of power each stage of a host can have. This is a ritual that the Hunter in darkness use to fix what they do.<br /> <br /> Or here is the gifts of Savagery, Agony, Scourging, Fervor and Disease from the pure. Some rituals they do.<br /> <br /> Here are the Balehounds, how they fit the new forsaken paradigm and what they hunt. Some powers they have.<br /> <br /> Fluff side an antagonist book could explore better how Tribe philosophy mesh with favored prey, that seems a little arbitrary on the core. What happens when a werewolf, for example follows the tennets of the storm lords but thinks the Pure are the most dangeorus prey and the Claimed the less important one?<br /> <br /> Explain the spiritual landscape better, i know they dont wanna redo previous material but the 1st edition core shouldnt be a necesary reading on top of the 2nd one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130599#post1130599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mostly because just releasing whole supplements of &quot;Oh, you've read this before, but now it's updated&quot; is kind of a boring point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats basically what Signs of Sorcery is, its Tome of Mysteries 2nd. Rules for souls, rules for Alchemy with some exploring on paths and rotecrafting (so its a mixture of Tome of Mystery + Grimoires + tome of the watchtowers). Sure, if you OPP doesnt wanna go the old supplement threadmill is fine but there is material that IS very needed for 2nd to be a somewhat round game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-17-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:09:39-07:00","id":1130648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130638#post1130638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats basically what Signs of Sorcery is, its Tome of Mysteries 2nd. Rules for souls, rules for Alchemy with some exploring on paths and rotecrafting (so its a mixture of Tome of Mystery + Grimoires + tome of the watchtowers). Sure, if you OPP doesnt wanna go the old supplement threadmill is fine but there is material that IS very needed for 2nd to be a somewhat round game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it's very clearly not. There's a ton of new stuff in there that's never even been tread upon before. THe concept of the book just happens to cover a fair amount of old territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:23:57-07:00","id":1130649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130648#post1130648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that it's very clearly not. There's a ton of new stuff in there that's never even been tread upon before. THe concept of the book just happens to cover a fair amount of old territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:25:30-07:00","id":1130650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130638#post1130638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The thing is while Chrod normally moves away from antagonist books, in the case of forsaken they should make an exception. The hunt is so much part of Forsaken that an antagonist book is needed.<br /> <br /> It is as if they had released Awakening and 4 arcanums werent in the book. Also if they wanna make the thematic naming, we got &quot;The pack&quot; and the next one should be &quot;The prey&quot;. You dont get more thematic than that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>4 Missing Arcana would make the game &quot;Mastigos: the Whatever&quot;, not Mage. I think you are exagerating here, because if this were the case, you simply wouldn't be able to play the game. This is untrue, as I know many people who play or played the game, and in a variety of themes even.<br /> <br /> I do not think you need a &quot;The Prey&quot; book to play (albeit I'd dig that). What I'd personally like is a &quot;The Hunt&quot; book, dealing not only with the targets of the prey, but the hunt in and of itself in more depth.<br /> But then, that is just me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:53:11-07:00","id":1130660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130650#post1130650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 Missing Arcana would make the game &quot;Mastigos: the Whatever&quot;, not Mage. I think you are exagerating here, because if this were the case, you simply wouldn't be able to play the game. This is untrue, as I know many people who play or played the game, and in a variety of themes even.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me in a way is that, is kinda the Blood Talon: Why we scare of the pure again? Or Hunter in Darkness: the fight the same 2 guys over and over again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130650#post1130650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think you need a &quot;The Prey&quot; book to play (albeit I'd dig that). What I'd personally like is a &quot;The Hunt&quot; book, dealing not only with the targets of the prey, but the hunt in and of itself in more depth.<br /> But then, that is just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or something that is barely covered, Challenges between packs, it almost a foot note in the 1st. Its barely mentioned everywhere else. Why choose any option beside might makes right? Types of challenges, examples, motives, etc.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130648#post1130648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that it's very clearly not. There's a ton of new stuff in there that's never even been tread upon before. THe concept of the book just happens to cover a fair amount of old territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>And said material is more or less stuff unique to 2nd and clarifications from the core. But it does convert all the relevant mechanics from Tome of Mysteries. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:10:16-07:00","id":1130671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130650#post1130650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not think you need a &quot;The Prey&quot; book to play (albeit I'd dig that). What I'd personally like is a &quot;The Hunt&quot; book, dealing not only with the targets of the prey, but the hunt in and of itself in more depth.<br /> But then, that is just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really liking this ''The Hunt'' idea. Although i didnt get the chance to run a werewolf game yet one thing that i've played with in my mind was atypical hunts (things beyond find target then kill it). One of those idea was for a storm lord who wanted to ''hunt'' a perceive weakness in another pack, but doing so without attacking directly the pack. The point being to rid this pack of the ''weakness''. But honestly i wouldnt even know where to begin to run that kind of hunt (mechanically speaking) or hell i dont even know if its a possible thing in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:22:19-07:00","id":1130677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130649#post1130649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Not the same thing a bit!' said the Hatter. 'You might just as well say that &quot;I see what I eat&quot; is the same thing as &quot;I eat what I see&quot;!'<br /> <br /> But seriously,.if that's your idea of same difference, then I assume you live a life delivered in halves alone. Signs of Sorcery's retread constitutes less than half of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:26:35-07:00","id":1130679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130660#post1130660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And said material is more or less stuff unique to 2nd and clarifications from the core. But it does convert all the relevant mechanics from Tome of Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> Signs of Sorcery [Mage: The Awakening] [Open Development] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, if so, then where is archmastery, Abyssal Spellcasting, a detailed discussion of the practices, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:33:11-07:00","id":1130681,"title":"","content":"Jesus just point towards the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">open development post</a>.<br /> <br /> Under 'What this book is not.'<br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tome of the Mysteries second edition. </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> It\u2019s not the only book we\u2019re revisiting content from. </span></span></span><b>Legacies: The Ancient</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> talks about perfected materials in the Forge Masters Legacy. </span></span></span><b>Tome of the Watchtowers</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> has an expanded table of Path symbols and the concept of dedications (which we have renamed while bringing back here.) </span></span></span><b>Grimoire of Grimoires</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> shows what the variety of rote texts should be, despite the seeming simplicity of the Scribe Grimoire spell. All of the Order books boast example Imbued Items and Artifacts. </span></span></span><b>Tome of the Mysteries</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, though, is the most-revisited. It\u2019s where 1e expanded on rotecraft, gave rules for Awakened alchemy, and talked about crafting. Every chapter includes some topics that were looked at previously, but as I imply above the writers were explicitly not beholden to prior interpretations; not everything that was appropriate for </span></span></span><b>Mage</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> back when </span></span></span><b>Tome of the Mysteries</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> was written is still so in a new edition, and especially in a book about Supernal Mysteries the cosmological changes we\u2019ve made to the game preclude some things from </span></span></span><i>ever</i><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> coming back while enabling others.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are clearly more books content is revisited from, but the writers weren't bound to it. This is as good a pitch as any for werewolf. Lodges were redone in a new and interesting way in the Pack, despite lodges having two books during first edition. As has been mentioned in plenty of posts, there are things we sorely need to be revisited for second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:42:49-07:00","id":1130685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130671#post1130671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really liking this ''The Hunt'' idea. Although i didnt get the chance to run a werewolf game yet one thing that i've played with in my mind was atypical hunts (things beyond find target then kill it). One of those idea was for a storm lord who wanted to ''hunt'' a perceive weakness in another pack, but doing so without attacking directly the pack. The point being to rid this pack of the ''weakness''. But honestly i wouldnt even know where to begin to run that kind of hunt (mechanically speaking) or hell i dont even know if its a possible thing in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have my core with me but i think the gifts of information/insight/hunting can help you with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130677#post1130677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of Sorcery's retread constitutes less than half of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what i gather signs of sorcery is<br /> Chapter One: The Supernal World which is newish as it doesnt interact with the new mage sight but i dont know how much is retread from Paths of the watchtower but lets say its all new.<br /> <br /> Chapter Two: The Mage\u2019s Tools. Newish because i am pretty sure Tome of mystery had a section of magical tool in it. Also the whole taking taboo thing from Tome of the watchtower.<br /> <br /> Chapter Three: The Crafter\u2019s Trade. All retread from tome of mysteries thats good. Alchemy, perfected materials and cursed items.<br /> <br /> Chapter Four: The Wealth of Knowledge. Lots of retreads. Rotes and advanced rotecraft, Grimoires, soul stones and annulities. Supposedly there will be new are rules for requisitions.<br /> <br /> Chapter Five: The Manifest Supernal. Artifacts, eidoforms, Sariras, Hallows, Verges, Emanation Realms, the creations of archmages, ruins of the Time Before, Ochemata, Ananke, and the Aeons, and secret people like Rmhoals.<br /> <br /> Now i havent read Imperial mysteries but i think a lot of those are already covered there. I do remember Ochemata being covered in Seers book and i know Imperial mysteries got the Archmages.<br /> <br /> Chapter Six: Awakening. Yup, all new.<br /> <br /> I wouldnt call it less than half the book is retreads. More like 50/50 or even 3/4 retread but i also dont consider retreads as something &quot;BAD!&quot; nor i understand why are &quot;BAD!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also is not the point on whether Signs of Sorcery is just a retread of Tome of mysteries or it also contains other retreads. The more conversions, the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-17-2017, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:47:32-07:00","id":1130687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130679#post1130679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorc...n-development/</a><br /> <br /> Also, if so, then where is archmastery, Abyssal Spellcasting, a detailed discussion of the practices, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that all of those were under the &quot;not everything that was appropriate for Mage back when Tome of the Mysteries was written is still so in a new edition&quot; on the archmastery and Abbysall spellcasting.<br /> <br /> As for the detailed discusion on practices. Isnt that coming in the FAQ that dave someday will release? <br /> <br /> EDIT: I went and check my copy of Tome of mysteries. Archmages are given 0 mechanics and are just given fluffy bits and a overview. I suppose that they were expanded on Imperial Mysteries. Also on the discussion on the practices wont that be covered on chapter 3 or 4 on rotecrafting on the whole mixing arcanums that lacked in the core? Abyssal magic is lacking true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-18-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:36:34-07:00","id":1130704,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't have a problem with the lack of content on the horizon, if it wasn't also that Werewolf had a long and silent dry spell during 1e.<br /> Yes, I know the limited lines have fewer books, but Werewolf wasn't designed as a limited line. I mean, it only got three more supplements than Changeling, which WAS a limited line.<br /> This silence combined with the fact that there are a few things missing is what worries me. Over-all I'm content. But there are two things I'd like to see:<br /> <br /> A villain-book. Not because we need to re-tread old ground, but because I have no idea how to update many of the antagonists to 2nd edition.<br /> I also want a high-end book. With stories and mechanics about the Deep Shadow and the gods and tribal totems that dwell there. First edition gave a few hints about endgame mechanics with the Milestone Gifts, and Aspects from Signs of the Moon. But they missed expanding the setting around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:53:27-07:00","id":1130710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130704#post1130704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A villain-book. Not because we need to re-tread old ground, but because I have no idea how to update many of the antagonists to 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my main problem with updating material from antagonists. For one the design idea on 1st was that power just concentrate on pumping the dicepool while second have more variety. And also aggravated damage. Werewolf doesnt have aggravated damage power because part of the hunt them is for them to find the weakness of the prey and exploit but what about antagonist and aggravated damage? Should they have it, shouldnt?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T04:53:28-07:00","id":1130774,"title":"","content":"All things aside, I gotta admit that as someone who fell in love with Forsaken because of Predators and read that book so many times I lost count, it is quite clear the book shows its age nowadays.<br /> <br /> I was talking about this with another fellow Werewolf fan the other day. It's not &quot;just&quot; the mechanics (though having new ones would be great for sure), it's also a matter of tone, lore and focus. Predators is an antagonist book written in early 1st Edition, where all the big three lines had a little problem of identity issues. Again, awesome book, but after 2nd Edition came in years later and sharpened the themes while rebuilding the setting, it also brought up the need to have detailed material about the antagonists which is up to par.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the gameline is abandoned or that other lines are to blame and all, I disagree with that line of thought and trust we'll get more stuff, but, if anything, we have to be fair and say that there's both need and demand for a book like that. Especially for a game like Werewolf were conflicts external to the characters are more frequent than in others. Hunters and preys, after all.<br /> <br /> (I want more about the Shartha, dammit)<br /> <br /> EDIT: (And just to be shameless, I'd be available to write those myself, Onyx Path. *wink*wink*)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-18-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:02:08-07:00","id":1131013,"title":"","content":"Lo and behold, the topic of dry spells get addressed at GenCon! TL;DR: They know that some lines have slowed down because of the need to updated everything to 2e, the brochure is not the be-all and end-all of what is coming this year, and there are a bunch of books that they have to pitch approval to nuWW. I haven't heard anything about WtF specifically yet, but already the panel has emphasized that they want to make sure every line gets something each year, even if it's via Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Forsaken game is not Forsaken! We are getting Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon! Ghost Wolves, the Pure, and Bale Hounds. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/gencon-2017-whats-up-with-white-wolf-rpgs/\" target=\"_blank\">CofD section starts at about 13:30.</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-18-2017, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:20:23-07:00","id":1131262,"title":"","content":"As Rich mentioned it at GenCon, I figured <a href=\"https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2017/stepping-back/\" target=\"_blank\">I should make it public</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>TL; DR: </b>Yes, I'm not developer any more. No, it's not to do with one line against the other. It's all to do with the amount of work at my day-job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:24:05-07:00","id":1131265,"title":"","content":"So, who <i>is</i> the developer now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T07:43:23-07:00","id":1131272,"title":"","content":"That's a question for Rich or Rose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:37:42-07:00","id":1131285,"title":"","content":"Chances are, they haven't figured it out yet.<br /> <br /> So, indeed, Forsaken has been patronless for over a year and half, by the former developer's own admission. Thanks for coming clean at least.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the lack of a developer for Forsaken must've fallen thru the cracks of 20+ projects. It's sorta eyebrow raising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-19-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:20:12-07:00","id":1131771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1130525#post1130525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's more, most of the money-making audience is in for exactly this stuff-if mechanics are a little sloppy, oh well, but if the setting goes wonky, LORD HELP YOU.(Most payers do not actually play the game, and instead enjoy these games as basically open fiction and daydream spaces)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my situation. Since I moved to Mexico when I married, I almost have not played neither storytelled. I buy the books for the joy of reading them. That doesnt mean I don't care for the rules, but the main joy for me is reading the setting, the &quot;fluff&quot; (as a non-english speaker, I just discovered recently that the term had a negative connotion, I always used it in a positive way). <br /> Even when I lived in Spain and bought absolutelly everything released from nWoD, I didn't use most of the material, I just bought it for the sake of reading it.<br /> <br /> I absolutelly loved Dark Eras for its fluff, and I loved Ancient Mysteries historical settings. And I hope to see more historical books for specyfic gamelines (as Eternal Flame for Hunter).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:24:10-07:00","id":1131772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131771#post1131771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the &quot;fluff&quot; (as a non-english speaker, I just discovered recently that the term had a negative connotion, I always used it in a positive way).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does? Damn, I did not know that and always used it neutrally for the same reason. Good to know.<br /> <br /> But yes, there are gamelines I don't ever think I'll run (one has the players one has) and I still get the books because I enjoy reading them. I like CoD's setting and fiction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:15:03-07:00","id":1131791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131772#post1131772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does? Damn, I did not know that and always used it neutrally for the same reason. Good to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the dictionary definition of the word &quot;fluff&quot; is something light and unsubstantive or something trivial and superficial. The later definition specifically refers to &quot;fluff articles&quot; in newspapers, which is a term for an article that doesn't have any real meaning and is only there to bump up a paper's word count. Hence why a number of RPG authors are not fans of the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:13:20-07:00","id":1131902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131262#post1131262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Rich mentioned it at GenCon, I figured <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2017/stepping-back/&amp;quot;]I</a> should make it public[/URL].<br /> <br /> <b>TL; DR: </b>Yes, I'm not developer any more. No, it's not to do with one line against the other. It's all to do with the amount of work at my day-job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sad to hear that, but as the rule goes: Real life comes first. Nothing but respect for what I assume was a hard decision.<br /> all the best to you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:19:59-07:00","id":1131905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131902#post1131902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sad to hear that, but as the rule goes: Real life comes first. Nothing but respect for what I assume was a hard decision.<br /> all the best to you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we got the memo a year and a half late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:37:13-07:00","id":1131915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131905#post1131905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we got the memo a year and a half late.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, just let it go? Maybe he didn't want to let go of W:tF, wasn't ready to admit it to himself? God knows that would have been me.<br /> That is all just conjecture, though. There are Hundes and one valid reasons, and another 101 understandable ones for things to go down like this.<br /> I get that this isn't ideal, but few things in life are.<br /> I for one am happy with what I get - more books- and got (because I really like 2ED werewolf more and more the more i read the book.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:28:43-07:00","id":1131956,"title":"","content":"I get the sentiment, but Malus has a point.<br /> <br /> We didn't have a developer for over a year and we didn't know about it. And while announcing a new book is good, especially since it's one that we've been wanting for years, 'we've been wanting it for years' and maybe it would be out by now if we had a new developer after Stew left. It might even be why Werewolf was missing from Thousand Years of Night's Crossover section.<br /> <br /> I really liked where Stew took things with Werewolf, but there's no one taking it anywhere now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:38:23-07:00","id":1131961,"title":"","content":"Well, what's done is done at this point.<br /> <br /> Bitching about it on forums isn't going to speed things along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:01:16-07:00","id":1131970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131961#post1131961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what's done is done at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's done is still going on at this point and until there's a new developer developing things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bitching about it on forums isn't going to speed things along. </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible his creating this thread is what brought the announcement that we had no developer up at a panel.<br /> <br /> I think buried among all the posts of disagreements and correcting of people, having one thread to complain is allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:11:45-07:00","id":1131975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131970#post1131970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think buried among all the posts of disagreements and correcting of people, having one thread to complain is allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and these books still aren't going to be released anytime soon. They're not coming out tomorrow, they're not coming out this month, and I'm pretty sure we're not going to see them before the end of 2017.<br /> <br /> I can wait. Got enough of a backlog of OPP books anyways I need to take care of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:08:20-07:00","id":1131997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131970#post1131970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible his creating this thread is what brought the announcement that we had no developer up at a panel.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I am generally on the side of just moving on, the quip about &quot;some people think that Werewolf the Forsaken truly has been forsaken&quot; from the panel would seem to indicate that they've read this thread. While I have no idea if it influenced their decision making process, the people's voices are at least being heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:15:59-07:00","id":1131998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131956#post1131956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the sentiment, but Malus has a point.<br /> <br /> We didn't have a developer for over a year and we didn't know about it. And while announcing a new book is good, especially since it's one that we've been wanting for years, 'we've been wanting it for years' and maybe it would be out by now if we had a new developer after Stew left. It might even be why Werewolf was missing from Thousand Years of Night's Crossover section.<br /> <br /> I really liked where Stew took things with Werewolf, but there's no one taking it anywhere now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a point is one thing, and good and fair. I might not see things the same way, and I am certain some of my interpretations of what I read are not entirely correct, so I apologize in advance for any assumptions and wrongful readings of you guys. Trapdoor of the medium due to lack of gestures, body language, voice pitch and similar signal, as well as this not being my first language, and despite being fairly proficient in it (I like to think so, at least) I still make some very stupid, sometimes funny, sometimes quite serious mistakes. I do not meant to attack anyone, and this is in response to you, but not at you. It is a general statement.<br /> <br /> So, with that out of the way:<br /> What would us knowing about there not being a developer have changed? Would it have sped up the process of finding someone to take over? I kind of doubt that. I think it wouldn't have done anything positive. There would have probably been less people willing to get into Werewolf, because 'it's been officially abandoned'. Maybe there might have been more threads about the fact that Forsaken is abandoned, about it 'not even having a developer'? Would that have helped? Again, personally, I doubt it.<br /> I am <i>not </i>denying complaints their space here, or questioning their rightfulness: being left in the dark sucks, especially when it is about something you care about. Especially when it is something you have felt weighing on you for a long time, finally being (sadly) proven right, possibly feeling betrayed. Letting out some steam occasionally is helpful, and if this thread indeed brought the announcement on, great, it served an additional purpose, it provided much needed clarity. But not being able to let go, bringing up the same point again and again, questioning those who, from my point of view, need support now more then ever... Maybe it is just me here, but it feels like losing sight of the big picture. Complaining about the splinter in your finger rather than pull it out. There is no catharsis involved for me here, it is just... dragging down? As good a word as any, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Are there reasons to not make something like this public? From an administrative and marketing standpoint, yes, many.<br /> Does it suck? Hell yeah it does. Is it okay to address mistakes or things one feels were handled poorly? It is of paramount importance that it is done! But there is a time, and a place for that. And maybe this is my cultural upbringing speaking, but if you address things, address them directly, openly, dont tiptoe around, don't make implications and leave them there. After all, you want to help ensure things work better in the future. At least, that should be your purpose when criticizing. In my opinion ( leave humble out, because it looks fake to me). And once you did that, things should be done. You should not retreat back and repeat the process. Because that is not helpful, nor healthy. For none of the involved.<br /> <br /> All that's left right now is dust off, clean up, and prepare shop for the next day.<br /> <br /> I might be overly optimistic or idealistic here, and if that is so, I apologize.<br /> And thank you for your understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.: Also, I hope Stew will still chime in for the line here and there, because I like where he took it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  didn't include a sentence I thought I did 08-20-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:51:47-07:00","id":1132008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131905#post1131905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we got the memo a year and a half late.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a large number of possible reasons why no word of this got out, several of which are much better than you'd think. Trust me, this is the sort of stuff I've been digging into for a bit now.<br /> <br /> As a related point, while a dedicated line developer may or may not be present, Werewolf has quite a few products pre-2E that came out under various developers, and there are a good number of highly dedicated writers who can make pitches, and probably will do so very actively now. We might even get a line dev out of one 'em, individual work schedules permitting. Hell, the Night Horrors book is an indicator that someone is distinctly looking out for the line.<br /> <br /> Some patience and trust ain't a bad thing. I get it's frustrating, and I'm not going to tell you not to be frustrated-but sometimes things look worse than they are, and time'll reveal if that's the case or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:10:41-07:00","id":1132017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would us knowing about there not being a developer have changed? Would it have sped up the process of finding someone to take over? I kind of doubt that. I think it wouldn't have done anything positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one i would say it would have shown a level of transparency that gives the customer (in this case, me) a sense of confidence on the company. For example, Catalyst game labs is a company whose shady deals have made it so that i dont trust anything they announce until its released and even then i wont put a cent on them until i have some sort of review that says &quot;it doesnt suck&quot;. Or in many cases i just dont buy it, recommend friend to also dont buy it or look for alternatives that dont give the company any money hoping the whole thing bankrupts and the IP goes to a better one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131915#post1131915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, just let it go? Maybe he didn't want to let go of W:tF, wasn't ready to admit it to himself? God knows that would have been me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131915#post1131915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there reasons to not make something like this public? From an administrative and marketing standpoint, yes, many.<br /> Does it suck? Hell yeah it does. Is it okay to address mistakes or things one feels were handled poorly? It is of paramount importance that it is done! But there is a time, and a place for that. And maybe this is my cultural upbringing speaking</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also my upbringing/current life speaking but a thing it bothers me isnt that the developer had to quit because other life obligation hadnt allow him to dedicate time for this but that they company let it reach that point. That they didnt just say &quot;look, you arent reaching deadlines so we gonna have to let you go&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am gonna admit that i have never worked on the publishing business but in any other job i have been part of when you stopped showing for work or couldnt make it to the deadlines, you get fired and someone else took your job. Again, i never worked on publishing business so i dont know the details involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-20-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:33:23-07:00","id":1132032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132017#post1132017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one i would say it would have shown a level of transparency that gives the customer (in this case, me) a sense of confidence on the company. For example, Catalyst game labs is a company whose shady deals have made it so that i dont trust anything they announce until its released and even then i wont put a cent on them until i have some sort of review that says &amp;quot;it doesnt suck&amp;quot;. Or in many cases i just dont buy it, recommend friend to also dont buy it or look for alternatives that dont give the company any money hoping the whole thing bankrupts and the IP goes to a better one. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is also my upbringing/current life speaking but a thing it bothers me isnt that the developer had to quit because other life obligation hadnt allow him to dedicate time for this but that they company let it reach that point. That they didnt just say &amp;quot;look, you arent reaching deadlines so we gonna have to let you go&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I am gonna admit that i have never worked on the publishing business but in any other job i have been part of when you stopped showing for work or couldnt made it to the deadlines, you get fired and someone else took your job. Again, i never worked on publishing business so i dont know the details involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I'm missing your point with these comments. Stew didn't quit or needed to be fired because any of his work wasn't working out. He let us know that his real world job was demanding more of his time and he didn't think he could be a dev anymore. So he wrapped up, and continues to wrap up, any books he had committed to developing. That's what you're supposed to do, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:41:20-07:00","id":1132034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132032#post1132032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I'm missing your point with these comments. Stew didn't quit or needed to be fired because any of his work wasn't working out. He let us know that his real world job was demanding more of his time and he didn't think he could be a dev anymore. So he wrapped up, and continues to wrap up, any books he had committed to developing. That's what you're supposed to do, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I though that the situation was that he wasnt able to be developer for werewolf (Forsaken) because of his real world job for a while (months) but that the he didnt officially step down as developer until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-20-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:54:11-07:00","id":1132036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131961#post1131961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what's done is done at this point.<br /> <br /> Bitching about it on forums isn't going to speed things along.</div> </div> </div> </div>A done point more than a year after the fact, a year and a half of aimlessness. It's kind of a long time. But I'll address that below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Blablablah</b><br /> <br /> What would us knowing about there not being a developer have changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Proved me right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it have spe<i>e</i>d up the process of finding someone to take over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of doubt that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it wouldn't have done anything positive. There would have probably been less people willing to get into Werewolf, because 'it's been officially abandoned'. Maybe there might have been more threads about the fact that Forsaken is abandoned, about it 'not even having a developer'? Would that have helped?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the state stuff is at now, so again, irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am <i>not </i>denying complaints their space here, or questioning their rightfulness: being left in the dark sucks, especially when it is about something you care about. Especially when it is something you have felt weighing on you for a long time, finally being (sadly) proven right, possibly feeling betrayed. Letting out some steam occasionally is helpful, and if this thread indeed brought the announcement on, great, it served an additional purpose</div> </div> </div> </div>Which do you think the purpose was? The original one. You thought it was just to bitch? No. It served it's purpose. Because when people complained they felt that Forsaken was being treated like a red haired stepchild of a line, folk would go &quot;but Dark Eras this, Dark Eras that&quot;. And pulling two books out of their asses (after reading that most of what we want is antagonists) without a developer the week with the most fan interaction by name dropping the stuff isn't going to magically divest me of that notion, neither it is playing puns with a genuine concern of the audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not being able to let go, bringing up the same point again and again, questioning those who, from my point of view, need support now more then ever... Maybe it is just me here, but it feels like losing sight of the big picture. Complaining about the splinter in your finger rather than pull it out. There is no catharsis involved for me here, it is just... dragging down? As good a word as any, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing this isn't your thread, then. I'll let it go when they show me who they hired to wear Stew's shoes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1131998#post1131998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there reasons to not make something like this public? From an administrative and marketing standpoint, yes, many.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant, doing seemingly no work in a year and a half to remedy the lack of projects won't fix the fact that people didn't do anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132008#post1132008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a large number of possible reasons why no word of this got out, several of which are much better than you'd think. Trust me, this is the sort of stuff I've been digging into for a bit now.<br /> <br /> As a related point, while a dedicated line developer may or may not be present, Werewolf has quite a few products pre-2E that came out under various developers, and there are a good number of highly dedicated writers who can make pitches, and probably will do so very actively now. We might even get a line dev out of one 'em, individual work schedules permitting. Hell, the Night Horrors book is an indicator that someone is distinctly looking out for the line.<br /> <br /> Some patience and trust ain't a bad thing. I get it's frustrating, and I'm not going to tell you not to be frustrated-but sometimes things look worse than they are, and time'll reveal if that's the case or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trusting, I've been patient for over a year, waiting for announcements where none would come. I've been in the Dark Eras bandwagon bashing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> ; they were proven right in the end. And I said it before: I'm thankful they came clean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:57:24-07:00","id":1132041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132034#post1132034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I though that the situation was that he wasnt able to be developer for werewolf (Forsaken) because of his real world job for a while (months) but that the he didnt officially step down as developer until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>We didn't mention it in public until now because now we have a couple of Forsaken books that we're ready to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:57:48-07:00","id":1132042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132032#post1132032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid I'm missing your point with these comments. Stew didn't quit or needed to be fired because any of his work wasn't working out. He let us know that his real world job was demanding more of his time and he didn't think he could be a dev anymore. So he wrapped up, and continues to wrap up, any books he had committed to developing. That's what you're supposed to do, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Stew has mentioned OPP that he need to be step down from main line developer 1,5 year ago - <b>Why new Forsaken line developer was not chosen to this date? </b>I understand that new line dev would not start his own project till Stew's end his ( maybe ), but it's rather long wait to find replacement, don't you think? And we still do not heard if there <i>is</i> any new Werewolf developer. If you have company and one of departments directors leave - you do not wait 1,5 year to find substitution worker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-21-2017, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:02:39-07:00","id":1132044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132042#post1132042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if Stew has mentioned OPP that he need to be step down from main line developer 1,5 year ago - Why new line developer was not chosen to this date? I understand that new line dev would not start his own project till Stew's end his ( maybe ), but it's rather long wait to find replecment, don't you think? If you have company and one of departments directors leave - you do not wait 1,5 year to find substituion worker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we didn't have new WtF books that needed a developer assigned. We knew we _would_ be getting to them, but other projects were on tap first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:08:46-07:00","id":1132046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132036#post1132036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A done point more than a year after the fact, a year and a half of aimlessness. It's kind of a long time. But I'll address that below.<br /> <br /> <br /> Proved me right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably.<br /> <br /> <br /> Irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is the state stuff is at now, so again, irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which do you think the purpose was? The original one. You thought it was just to bitch? No. It served it's purpose. Because when people complained they felt that Forsaken was being treated like a red haired stepchild of a line, folk would go &amp;quot;but Dark Eras this, Dark Eras that&amp;quot;. And pulling two books out of their asses (after reading that most of what we want is antagonists) without a developer the week with the most fan interaction by name dropping the stuff isn't going to magically divest me of that notion, neither it is playing puns with a genuine concern of the audience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good thing this isn't your thread, then. I'll let it go when they show me who they hired to wear Stew's shoes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Irrelevant, doing seemingly no work in a year and a half to remedy the lack of projects won't fix the fact that people didn't do anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've been trusting, I've been patient for over a year, waiting for announcements where none would come. I've been in the Dark Eras bandwagon bashing <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> ; they were proven right in the end. And I said it before: I'm thankful they came clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of why announce the new WtF books now, you're putting the cart before the horse. I had my list made up of what we were announcing before I left for GenCon. As I've mentioned in general in Monday Meeting Blogs since the beginning of the year, we had some internal restructuring to do, and once that got done, it was time to get some more books announced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:13:25-07:00","id":1132048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132044#post1132044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we didn't have new WtF books that needed a developer assigned. We knew we _would_ be getting to them, but other projects were on tap first.</div> </div> </div> </div>But looking for main developer should be <i>before</i> assigning books, so he could prepare to writing them - and lead line development. Also, is it not main line's developer responsibility to propose OPP ideas for next books in the first place? Like <b>DaveB</b> comes with Mage books ideas to you guys?<br /> <br /> We still do not know IF Forsaken has line developer now, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:20:12-07:00","id":1132051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132036#post1132036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A done point more than a year after the fact, a year and a half of aimlessness. It's kind of a long time. But I'll address that below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> I've since settled into the KS books' cycle of the KS being put up, and then the book being released 1.5-2 years later.<br /> <br /> Nothing unusual there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:23:57-07:00","id":1132053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132046#post1132046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of why announce the new WtF books now, you're putting the cart before the horse. I had my list made up of what we were announcing before I left for GenCon. As I've mentioned in general in Monday Meeting Blogs since the beginning of the year, we had some internal restructuring to do, and once that got done, it was time to get some more books announced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one had faith that Onyx Path wasn't going to abandon any of their lines 'by choice'. I am sorry that you keep getting these insulting and offensive accusations. Heck, I am a fan of Geist the Sineaters (the least 'supported' of the Chronicles/NWoD lines) and I know it is not out of malice or favouritism. Life is complicated and I know you and everyone at OPP and WW have them.<br /> <br /> It is okay. I have been guilty in the past of worrying if you are going to shut down, but I don't imagine that would be pleasant for you all either. I am sorry if I have ever made you or any of the writers, editors or developers feel bad about your work, the creation of new content or the lack there of. This is something I feel you and the others don't hear enough: positive acknowledgement of your work and appreciation. Not everyone is blaming you for failing to meet their expectations and fears that it will spell the end of the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:30:00-07:00","id":1132056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132051#post1132051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really.<br /> <br /> I've since settled into the KS books' cycle of the KS being put up, and then the book being released 1.5-2 years later.<br /> <br /> Nothing unusual there.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about a kickstarter. Hell, I'd love to see one for a Forsaken product. We're talking about a line being left to it's own devices for more than a year. Nevermind the announced Secret of the Tribes, the year before that got left conspicuously out of this year's brochure. Because we had no developer dedicated to it. What would've happened if we did? Don't answer, that's rhetorical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:33:22-07:00","id":1132057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132048#post1132048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But looking for main developer should be <i>before</i> assigning books, so he could prepare to writing them - and lead line development. Also, is it not main line's developer responsibility to propose OPP ideas for next books in the first place? Like <b>DaveB</b> comes with Mage books ideas to you guys?<br /> <br /> We still do not know IF Forsaken has line developer now, even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. We've certainly done things that way for some lines. And sometimes we haven't. In terms of pitches, any of our developers, and often writers, can pitch an idea for a line. It's not restricted to only the developer of that game line. And sometimes I'll say that we need a particular book or kind of book and then we'll flesh that out with the developer. None of these methods, or more, are &quot;wrong&quot; so long as you end up with a really good book in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:34:06-07:00","id":1132058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132056#post1132056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not talking about a kickstarter. Hell, I'd love to see one for a Forsaken product. We're talking about a line being left to it's own devices for more than a year. Nevermind the announced Secret of the Tribes, the year before that got left conspicuously out of this year's brochure. Because we had no developer dedicated to it. What would've happened if we did? Don't answer, that's rhetorical.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and it was just a year. So what?<br /> <br /> There's enough games out there, even in CofD, that I don't feel the need to be waiting on bated breath for the fate of one gameline. Kinda like expanding my horizons.<br /> <br /> I'd be more concerned if it was +5 years and no movement or official statement was made about the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:39:10-07:00","id":1132061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132056#post1132056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not talking about a kickstarter. Hell, I'd love to see one for a Forsaken product. We're talking about a line being left to it's own devices for more than a year. Nevermind the announced Secret of the Tribes, the year before that got left conspicuously out of this year's brochure. Because we had no developer dedicated to it. What would've happened if we did? Don't answer, that's rhetorical.</div> </div> </div> </div>A LOT of upcoming projects were left out of the brochure this year. Deliberately, because we weren't trying to give a list of books to expect the coming year, but to suggest that they are &quot;in queue&quot; to be worked on. Again, you might be putting cart before horse: when we're ready to start producing the next WtF book is when we'll look for a developer for it. Maybe that person will continue and develop more WtF books, maybe not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:42:08-07:00","id":1132062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132056#post1132056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not talking about a kickstarter. Hell, I'd love to see one for a Forsaken product. We're talking about a line being left to it's own devices for more than a year. Nevermind the announced Secret of the Tribes, the year before that got left conspicuously out of this year's brochure. Because we had no developer dedicated to it. What would've happened if we did? Don't answer, that's rhetorical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the new books announced at GenCon weren't in the brochure this year. Rich talked about Tribes of the Moon still being upcoming in panel, right before he announced the new Night Horrors book. Tribes being &quot;conspicuously&quot; left out of the brochure means squat.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by Rich himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:44:01-07:00","id":1132063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132061#post1132061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you might be putting cart before horse: when we're ready to start producing the next WtF book is when we'll look for a developer for it. Maybe that person will continue and develop more WtF books, maybe not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Forsaken will not have main line developer guy, just many 'I will write one chapter on this' guys? Well, that's assuring... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:45:03-07:00","id":1132064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132053#post1132053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I for one had faith that Onyx Path wasn't going to abandon any of their lines 'by choice'. I am sorry that you keep getting these insulting and offensive accusations. Heck, I am a fan of Geist the Sineaters (the least 'supported' of the Chronicles/NWoD lines) and I know it is not out of malice or favouritism. Life is complicated and I know you and everyone at OPP and WW have them.<br /> <br /> It is okay. I have been guilty in the past of worrying if you are going to shut down, but I don't imagine that would be pleasant for you all either. I am sorry if I have ever made you or any of the writers, editors or developers feel bad about your work, the creation of new content or the lack there of. This is something I feel you and the others don't hear enough: positive acknowledgement of your work and appreciation. Not everyone is blaming you for failing to meet their expectations and fears that it will spell the end of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never assumed it was everyone, but still, it is very nice of you to post it. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:48:39-07:00","id":1132065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132063#post1132063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Forsaken will not have main line developer guy, just many 'I will write one chapter on this' guys? Well, that's assuring... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering some of those guys are people you've openly been excited for?<br /> <br /> Stop looking for clouds, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:49:04-07:00","id":1132066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132063#post1132063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Forsaken will not have main line developer guy, just many 'I will write one chapter on this' guys? Well, that's assuring... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not at all what I said. I was pretty specifically talking about book developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:58:57-07:00","id":1132068,"title":"","content":"Do remember that Vampire didn't get a book for 3 years. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T22:00:45-07:00","id":1132070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca