hunned by the Moon. It's happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, waiting then for something more substenstial than 'we are doing this' - or for pointing new line developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T23:17:49-07:00","id":1132097,"title":"","content":"Yes yes, we should be happy with what we have, we got it the first round when folks were denying there was a problem, we get it now when you say the problem isn't a problem anymore. We get the gist of what you are saying.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic. Rich posted <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/heres-the-windup-and-the-pitch-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, to explain the process of pitch season and how books are made, and these two books seem like pitches.<br /> <br /> Considering they're announced I'd guess they're after this point.<br /> <br /> 'At this point, I\u2019ll create a run down that gives the short reasons for why each project is needed and cool, and submit that to our license owners; at this time the new White Wolf Publishing. We haven\u2019t actually done this for new projects yet, so fingers crossed for this first \u201cschedule\u201d approval.'<br /> <br /> And the next stages seem to heavily require a developer, which we don't have or hasn't been announced. I'd put up a vote for Chris, but our last petition didn't go over too well..<br /> <br /> And so, since Rich is pretty open to questions in the Monday Meeting blog posts and I expect that would be a better place to ask him things, especially considering how this thread is going. I plan on asking how line developers are chosen, if Forsaken has one, and if a line has had books come out without having a line developer before, and how that turned out. If anyone has questions for him it seems like a good place to ask him on Monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-21-2017, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T00:16:17-07:00","id":1132112,"title":"","content":"Mage didn't have a line developer between Bill Bridges and myself - about half of first edition. Each book was done individually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:32:58-07:00","id":1132136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132112#post1132112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage didn't have a line developer between Bill Bridges and myself - about half of first edition. Each book was done individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that before or after OPP was a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:36:51-07:00","id":1132137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132097#post1132097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the next stages seem to heavily require a developer, which we don't have or hasn't been announced. I'd put up a vote for Chris, but our last petition didn't go over too well..<br /> <br /> And so, since Rich is pretty open to questions in the Monday Meeting blog posts and I expect that would be a better place to ask him things, especially considering how this thread is going. I plan on asking how line developers are chosen, if Forsaken has one, and if a line has had books come out without having a line developer before, and how that turned out. If anyone has questions for him it seems like a good place to ask him on Monday.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened in the last petition?<br /> <br /> You know what, that sounds like a fantastic idea! I'd really like to read more about that kind of stuff, that kind of behind-the-scenes peek would be very interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:40:49-07:00","id":1132139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132136#post1132136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that before or after OPP was a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Before. It's not that unusual. And Rose still oversees all Chronicles books, so there <i>is</i> a big-picture set of eyes on every book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T03:37:17-07:00","id":1132147,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that perhaps there's some confusion between roles...<br /> <br /> A line developer isn't a necessity for a game. It's a good thing to have, don't get me wrong, but many games have gone multiple years without them. A line developer pitches ideas along with the writers, and generally has a sense of the line as a whole and where things fit. Each <i>book</i> has a developer, who writes an outline, hires freelancers, and makes the best book they can. While line developers usually \u2014 but not always* \u2014 end up being the book developers for the books in their line. It is not just possible but <i>common</i> for lines to have books produced by different developers, under the guiding hands of Rich and Rose, without a line developer.<br /> <br /> I didn't announce this earlier because I was and am committed to finishing the books I had in progress, and it'd cause more problems than it solved. Hell, I was still developing <b>The Pack</b>. I'm absolutely certain that if I'd said something at the time, we would see threads like this worrying about the status of that book, despite me being clear that I was going to finish it. We've got new books on the way, <br /> <br /> New books are coming. They'll likely come <i>faster</i> because they've got developers who can give them the time and attention that they deserve. Rose oversees all Chronicles of Darkness books, so it's not like we don't have continuity between books. This is a <i>good time</i> for <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>.<br /> <br /> * For example: Bill Bridges was the developer for <b>W20: Kinfolk</b> even as I was still <b>W20</b> line developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:15:12-07:00","id":1132175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132083#post1132083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We got confirmation on <b>Night Horrors: The Shauned by Moon</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If Edgar Wright and Simon Pegg aren't involved, I will be sorely disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:37:21-07:00","id":1132185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132041#post1132041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We didn't mention it in public until now because now we have a couple of Forsaken books that we're ready to create.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132044#post1132044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because we didn't have new WtF books that needed a developer assigned. We knew we _would_ be getting to them, but other projects were on tap first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, as i said i havent ever worked on publishing so i though it was the other way around, that the lack of developer was the thing stopped the assignment of new Forsaken books. Instead of the lack of new assignment forsaken books being the reason the Developer issue wasnt addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:45:23-07:00","id":1132190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132147#post1132147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that perhaps there's some confusion between roles...<br /> <br /> A line developer isn't a necessity for a game. It's a good thing to have, don't get me wrong, but many games have gone multiple years without them. A line developer pitches ideas along with the writers, and generally has a sense of the line as a whole and where things fit. Each <i>book</i> has a developer, who writes an outline, hires freelancers, and makes the best book they can. While line developers usually \u2014 but not always* \u2014 end up being the book developers for the books in their line. It is not just possible but <i>common</i> for lines to have books produced by different developers, under the guiding hands of Rich and Rose, without a line developer.<br /> <br /> I didn't announce this earlier because I was and am committed to finishing the books I had in progress, and it'd cause more problems than it solved. Hell, I was still developing <b>The Pack</b>. I'm absolutely certain that if I'd said something at the time, we would see threads like this worrying about the status of that book, despite me being clear that I was going to finish it. We've got new books on the way, <br /> <br /> New books are coming. They'll likely come <i>faster</i> because they've got developers who can give them the time and attention that they deserve. Rose oversees all Chronicles of Darkness books, so it's not like we don't have continuity between books. This is a <i>good time</i> for <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>.<br /> <br /> * For example: Bill Bridges was the developer for <b>W20: Kinfolk</b> even as I was still <b>W20</b> line developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thank you dearly for that Information. If this does not clear up the rest of the confusion, nothing will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T07:06:44-07:00","id":1132199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132112#post1132112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage didn't have a line developer between Bill Bridges and myself - about half of first edition. Each book was done individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you happen to know which book was his last, as line developer? I think all I know of their publishing order was one of the Tomes came first and Left Hand Path and Imperial Mysteries came near the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132137#post1132137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened in the last petition?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title\">Nothing.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132147#post1132147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't announce this earlier because I was and am committed to finishing the books I had in progress, and it'd cause more problems than it solved. Hell, I was still developing The Pack. I'm absolutely certain that if I'd said something at the time, we would see threads like this worrying about the status of that book, despite me being clear that I was going to finish it. We've got new books on the way,<br /> <br /> New books are coming. They'll likely come <i>faster</i> because they've got developers who can give them the time and attention that they deserve. Rose oversees all Chronicles of Darkness books, so it's not like we don't have continuity between books. This is a <i>good time</i> for <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>These books have developers at the moment? Secrets of the Tribes and Shunned by the Moon? Or do you mean when developers are assigned to them?<br /> <br /> Also, wasn't there supposed to be web content that came with the Pack?<br /> <br /> I guess on this point I'm unclear on why it's a good time right now. I get that not having a line developer isn't a dealbreaker, or the end of the world, though we'll miss your guiding hand. But Secrets of the Tribes was announced a while back at a GenCon and didn't come out, for instance, so Shunned by the Moon can be just like that, something in the nebulous future which may take a handful of months to get from started to finish but may take years to get to that point.<br /> <br /> Basically, will we be having this same thread after the next GenCon, with these books still on a potential schedule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-21-2017, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T08:12:47-07:00","id":1132219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132199#post1132199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These books have developers at the moment? Secrets of the Tribes and Shunned by the Moon? Or do you mean when developers are assigned to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if they have developers or not. But since they've been announced, I'd not be surprised that Rich and/or Rose have developers in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, wasn't there supposed to be web content that came with the Pack? </div> </div> </div>No, there wasn't &quot;supposed to be&quot; anything. Some additional content for The Pack was mooted by one of the writers and I was giving it a once-over, but it fell by the wayside again because of day-job concerns. Stuff on the website like that is <i>never guaranteed</i>. At best it's a nice-to-have, but there is no obligation on either writers or developers to provide it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess on this point I'm unclear on why it's a good time right now. I get that not having a line developer isn't a dealbreaker, or the end of the world, though we'll miss your guiding hand. But Secrets of the Tribes was announced a while back at a GenCon and didn't come out, for instance, so Shunned by the Moon can be just like that, something in the nebulous future which may take a handful of months to get from started to finish but may take years to get to that point.<br /> <br /> Basically, will we be having this same thread after the next GenCon, with these books still on a potential schedule? </div> </div> </div>I'd put my money on &quot;you won't be having the same thread next year&quot;. I'm not going to say anything for certain, given my lack of involvement, but to reiterate: having developers who have the time to dedicate to the books means that they will happen faster once they are underway. I can't (or rather, I would but I won't) count the number of weeks that I <i>thought</i> I would have time to make progress on a book but ended up doing only a fraction of what I wanted to \u2014 if anything at all \u2014 because of outside factors, but another developer won't have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T05:44:06-07:00","id":1132568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132078#post1132078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Shunned by the Moon could have a production cycle similar to Enemy Action, which has gone from Frist Drafts to Development in 3 months and could easily be out within 6 months of us first knowing about it.<br /> <br /> You're panicking Wyrd, you need to chill out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seriously. Some of the comments here also make me think that there's some confusion about what a &quot;developer&quot; does. <br /> <br /> I developed <b>Mage</b> books for a while, but I was never the line developer. I was <i>a</i> developer (insofar as I knew the process) who developed some <b>Mage</b> books (because I'd worked pretty extensively on the line). Joe Carriker, Bill Bridges, and Stephen DiPesa also developed <b>Mage</b> books during the same rough period. <br /> <br /> This has also happened with <b>Werewolf</b>, <b>Vampire</b>, and &quot;blue books.&quot; The smaller lines have had more consistent devs (I've done almost all of the development for <b>Promethean</b>, but that's as much to do with how little there's been as anything else). None of us actually work for OPP, we're hired on a freelance basis, so saying that anyone is a &quot;line developer&quot; is true only as far as Rich and Rose wants to keep hiring a particular developer for projects in the same line. Rich could decide tomorrow that he doesn't like the cut of my jib and hire someone else for the next <b>Promethean</b> book (<i>there's gonna be another one, right, Rich? Please?</i>), and while that would be sad, it's also totally above-board. <br /> <br /> Similarly, if another such book comes around and I say &quot;you know what, I'd love to but I'm snowed under developing <b>Chill</b> and writing <b>Timepeekers</b>&quot;, Rich would hire someone else to dev said book, and that would be fine. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:14:15-07:00","id":1132849,"title":"","content":"Since I kickstarted Chill I'm always happy to see low-key plugs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T10:40:46-07:00","id":1133078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1130344-abandoned-game-is-abandoned?p=1132849#post1132849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I kickstarted Chill I'm always happy to see low-key plugs</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd have linked to our new <b>Chill</b> book, but that seemed a little gauche. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}